PathwayData.put("data/reading_writing/units/L05U4.json",{"strand":"reading_writing","level":5,"cefr":"B1a","unit":4,"theme":"Heroes Around Us","essential_question":"What makes someone a hero?","schema_version":"1.0","core_words":["courage","rescue","sacrifice","integrity","determined","inspire","admire","achievement","challenge","overcome","role model","responsibility","humble","selfless"],"recycled_words":["brave","kind","honest","help","neighbor","grandmother","theme","trait","simile","metaphor","for example","letter","dream"],"rubrics":[{"id":"RW-RUBRIC-5T","title":"Analytic writing rubric","traits":[{"name":"Ideas","name_ar":"الأفكار","bands":[{"score":4,"descriptor":"My ideas are clear, interesting and fully developed with strong details.","descriptor_ar":"أفكاري واضحة وممتعة ومدعومة بتفاصيل قوية."},{"score":3,"descriptor":"My ideas are clear and have enough details.","descriptor_ar":"أفكاري واضحة ومعها تفاصيل كافية."},{"score":2,"descriptor":"My main idea is there but needs more details.","descriptor_ar":"فكرتي الرئيسية موجودة لكنها تحتاج إلى تفاصيل أكثر."},{"score":1,"descriptor":"My ideas are unclear or very few.","descriptor_ar":"أفكاري غير واضحة أو قليلة جدًا."}]},{"name":"Organization","name_ar":"التنظيم","bands":[{"score":4,"descriptor":"Clear beginning, middle and end; ideas flow with linking words.","descriptor_ar":"بداية ووسط ونهاية واضحة، والأفكار مترابطة بكلمات الربط."},{"score":3,"descriptor":"Clear order with some linking words.","descriptor_ar":"ترتيب واضح مع بعض كلمات الربط."},{"score":2,"descriptor":"Some order, but parts are mixed up.","descriptor_ar":"يوجد بعض الترتيب لكن بعض الأجزاء غير مرتبة."},{"score":1,"descriptor":"Ideas are not in order.","descriptor_ar":"الأفكار غير مرتبة."}]},{"name":"Vocabulary","name_ar":"المفردات","bands":[{"score":4,"descriptor":"I use exact, varied words, including new unit words, correctly.","descriptor_ar":"أستخدم كلمات دقيقة ومتنوعة، منها كلمات الوحدة الجديدة، بشكل صحيح."},{"score":3,"descriptor":"I use some new words correctly.","descriptor_ar":"أستخدم بعض الكلمات الجديدة بشكل صحيح."},{"score":2,"descriptor":"I use simple words; some are repeated or wrong.","descriptor_ar":"أستخدم كلمات بسيطة، وبعضها مكرر أو غير صحيح."},{"score":1,"descriptor":"I use very few words; the meaning is hard to understand.","descriptor_ar":"أستخدم كلمات قليلة جدًا ويصعب فهم المعنى."}]},{"name":"Sentence fluency","name_ar":"سلاسة الجمل","bands":[{"score":4,"descriptor":"My sentences are complete, varied in length and easy to read aloud.","descriptor_ar":"جملي كاملة ومتنوعة الطول وسهلة القراءة بصوت عالٍ."},{"score":3,"descriptor":"Most sentences are complete, with some variety.","descriptor_ar":"معظم جملي كاملة مع بعض التنويع."},{"score":2,"descriptor":"Many sentences are short or start the same way.","descriptor_ar":"كثير من جملي قصيرة أو تبدأ بالطريقة نفسها."},{"score":1,"descriptor":"Sentences are incomplete or run together.","descriptor_ar":"جملي ناقصة أو متداخلة."}]},{"name":"Conventions","name_ar":"قواعد الكتابة","bands":[{"score":4,"descriptor":"Capitals, punctuation, spelling and grammar are almost always correct.","descriptor_ar":"الحروف الكبيرة وعلامات الترقيم والإملاء والقواعد صحيحة دائمًا تقريبًا."},{"score":3,"descriptor":"A few mistakes that do not affect meaning.","descriptor_ar":"أخطاء قليلة لا تؤثر في المعنى."},{"score":2,"descriptor":"Several mistakes; the meaning is sometimes unclear.","descriptor_ar":"عدة أخطاء، والمعنى أحيانًا غير واضح."},{"score":1,"descriptor":"Many mistakes make it hard to read.","descriptor_ar":"أخطاء كثيرة تجعل القراءة صعبة."}]}]}],"lessons":[{"id":"RW-L05-U4-LS1","title":"Word Power: Heroes Around Us","lesson_type":"vocabulary","objectives":["read, say and use 14 words about heroes and character and 4 Tier 2 words (demonstrate, contribute, motivate, persevere)","understand shades of meaning: words with similar meanings but different strengths (brave → bold → fearless)","choose the most exact word for a sentence"],"objectives_ar":["قراءة ونطق واستخدام 14 كلمة عن الأبطال والشخصية و4 كلمات أكاديمية.","فهم درجات المعنى: كلمات متقاربة المعنى مختلفة القوة.","اختيار الكلمة الأدق للجملة."],"success_criteria":["I can use the hero words correctly in sentences.","I can order similar words from weakest to strongest.","I can explain why one word fits a sentence better than another."],"success_criteria_ar":["أستطيع استخدام كلمات البطولة في جمل بشكل صحيح.","أستطيع ترتيب الكلمات المتقاربة من الأضعف إلى الأقوى.","أستطيع شرح لماذا تناسب كلمةٌ الجملةَ أكثر من غيرها."],"map_area":"Vocabulary: Acquisition and Use","vocabulary":[{"word":"courage","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈkɝɪdʒ/","definition":"the ability to do something difficult or frightening","arabic":"شجاعة","example":"It took courage to help in the storm.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V01","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V01","tier":"core"},{"word":"rescue","pos":"verb / noun","ipa":"/ˈrɛskju/","definition":"to save someone from danger","arabic":"ينقذ / إنقاذ","example":"The team rescued the old man.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V02","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V02","tier":"core"},{"word":"sacrifice","pos":"noun / verb","ipa":"/ˈsækrəˌfaɪs/","definition":"giving up something important to help others","arabic":"تضحية / يضحّي","example":"Doctors make sacrifices to help patients.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V03","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V03","tier":"core"},{"word":"integrity","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ɪnˈtɛɡrəti/","definition":"being honest and doing what is right, even when no one is watching","arabic":"النزاهة","example":"A person with integrity tells the truth.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V04","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V04","tier":"core"},{"word":"determined","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/dɪˈtɝmɪnd/","definition":"not willing to give up","arabic":"مصمّم / عازم","example":"She was determined to finish the race.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V05","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V05","tier":"core"},{"word":"inspire","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ɪnˈspaɪər/","definition":"to make someone want to do something good or great","arabic":"يُلهم","example":"Her story inspired me to study science.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V06","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V06","tier":"core"},{"word":"admire","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ədˈmaɪər/","definition":"to respect and like someone for what they are or do","arabic":"يُعجب بـ / يقدّر","example":"I admire my grandfather's patience.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V07","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V07","tier":"core"},{"word":"achievement","pos":"noun","ipa":"/əˈtʃivmənt/","definition":"something great that you succeed in doing","arabic":"إنجاز","example":"Going to space was a great achievement.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V08","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V08","tier":"core"},{"word":"challenge","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈtʃælɪndʒ/","definition":"something difficult that tests your ability","arabic":"تحدٍّ","example":"Learning a new language is a challenge.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V09","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V09","tier":"core"},{"word":"overcome","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˌoʊvərˈkʌm/","definition":"to succeed in dealing with a problem or a fear","arabic":"يتغلّب على","example":"Sami overcame his fear of storms.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V10","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V10","tier":"core"},{"word":"role model","pos":"noun","ipa":"/roʊl ˈmɑdəl/","definition":"a person you want to be like","arabic":"قدوة","example":"My teacher is my role model.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V11","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V11","tier":"core"},{"word":"responsibility","pos":"noun","ipa":"/rɪˌspɑnsəˈbɪləti/","definition":"a duty to take care of someone or something","arabic":"مسؤولية","example":"Looking after my sister is my responsibility.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V12","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V12","tier":"core"},{"word":"humble","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈhʌmbəl/","definition":"not thinking you are better than other people","arabic":"متواضع","example":"The hero was humble and said, 'I just helped.'","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V13","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V13","tier":"core"},{"word":"selfless","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈsɛlflɪs/","definition":"caring more about other people than about yourself","arabic":"مُؤْثِر / غير أناني","example":"The volunteer was selfless and worked all night.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V14","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V14","tier":"core"},{"word":"demonstrate","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˈdɛmənˌstreɪt/","definition":"to show something clearly","arabic":"يُظهر / يبرهن","example":"He demonstrated great courage.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V15","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V15","tier":"tier2"},{"word":"contribute","pos":"verb","ipa":"/kənˈtrɪbjut/","definition":"to give or do something to help a group","arabic":"يسهم","example":"Everyone can contribute to a cleaner school.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V16","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V16","tier":"tier2"},{"word":"motivate","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˈmoʊtəˌveɪt/","definition":"to make someone want to try hard","arabic":"يحفّز","example":"My coach motivates me to practice.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V17","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V17","tier":"tier2"},{"word":"persevere","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˌpɝsəˈvɪr/","definition":"to keep trying even when something is difficult","arabic":"يثابر","example":"She persevered and finally passed the test.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V18","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V18","tier":"tier2"}],"explanation":{"text":"Some words have **similar meanings** but different **strengths** or **feelings**. We call these **shades of meaning** – like light blue, blue and dark blue.\n\nExamples from weakest to strongest: **brave → bold → fearless**; **nervous → scared → terrified**; **glad → happy → thrilled**; **tired → exhausted**; **like → admire → idolize**. Some words also have a different **feeling**: *bold* can sound a little rude, but *brave* is always positive.\n\nTo choose the best word: (1) think about **how strong** the feeling or action is; (2) look at the **context** (who, what, how much); (3) try each word in the sentence and choose the one that is **most exact**.","examples":["*Sami was **nervous** before his first speech.* → a small worry.","*Sami was **scared** when the lights went out.* → more fear.","*Lama was **terrified** and screamed.* → very strong fear.","*The firefighter was **brave**.* → has courage.","*She was **fearless**; she ran into the smoke without stopping.* → shows no fear at all.","*I was **glad** the rain stopped. / I was **thrilled** when we won the cup!* → weak vs. very strong happiness.","*After the long rescue, the team was **exhausted**.* → stronger than tired.","*I **admire** my grandmother* (respect) – stronger than *I like my grandmother's food*.","Order them: **warm → hot → boiling**; **walk → hurry → race**; **look → stare**."],"common_errors":["✗ I was terrified when I forgot my pencil. → ✓ I was a little worried when I forgot my pencil. (Too strong for a small problem.)","✗ The rescue was a little brave. → ✓ The rescuers were very brave. (Match the strength to the action.)","✗ Using 'very very scared'. → ✓ Use one exact word: terrified. (A strong word is better than 'very very'.)","✗ He overcomed his fear. → ✓ He overcame his fear. (Irregular past: **overcame**.)","✗ She is a role model for me to admire her. → ✓ She is my role model. / I admire her. (Keep it simple.)","✗ He was determinate. → ✓ He was determined. (Adjective: **determined**.)","✗ She persevered to give up. → ✓ She persevered and didn't give up. (persevere = keep trying.)"],"arabic":"بعض الكلمات متقاربة المعنى لكنها مختلفة القوة أو الشعور، وتُسمّى درجات المعنى، مثل الأزرق الفاتح والأزرق والأزرق الغامق.\n\nأمثلة من الأضعف إلى الأقوى: brave ← bold ← fearless، وnervous ← scared ← terrified، وglad ← happy ← thrilled.\n\nلاختيار الكلمة الأفضل: فكّر في قوة الشعور أو الفعل، وانظر إلى السياق، وجرّب كل كلمة واختر الأدق.\n\nانتبه: overcome ماضيها overcame، والصفة determined."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:25","narration":"Not all heroes wear capes. Some carry flashlights, stethoscopes or school bags!","on_screen":"Heroes Around Us 🦸","visual":"A nurse, a firefighter, a teacher and a child with a flashlight stand together."},{"time":"00:25–01:20","narration":"Heroes show courage, integrity and responsibility. They are selfless and humble. They rescue, inspire and overcome challenges!","on_screen":"courage · integrity · responsibility · selfless · humble · rescue · inspire · overcome · challenge","visual":"Quick scenes of everyday heroes."},{"time":"01:20–01:55","narration":"We admire role models for their achievements and their sacrifices – and they motivate us to persevere and contribute!","on_screen":"admire · role model · achievement · sacrifice · determined · demonstrate · contribute · motivate · persevere","visual":"A girl looks at a poster of an astronaut."},{"time":"01:55–03:05","narration":"Shades of meaning! Nervous, scared, terrified. Brave, bold, fearless. Glad, happy, thrilled!","on_screen":"weak → strong 🎨","visual":"Paint strips go from light to dark as the words get stronger."},{"time":"03:05–03:30","narration":"Choose the most exact word – it makes your writing powerful!","on_screen":"Exact words = strong writing","visual":"A pencil chooses 'terrified' over 'very very scared'."}],"captions_ar":["ليس كل الأبطال يرتدون العباءات؛ بعضهم يحمل مصباحًا أو سماعة طبيب أو حقيبة مدرسية!","الأبطال يُظهرون الشجاعة والنزاهة والمسؤولية، ويؤثرون غيرهم ويتواضعون، وينقذون ويُلهمون ويتغلبون على التحديات!","نُعجب بالقدوات لإنجازاتهم وتضحياتهم، فهم يحفزوننا على المثابرة والإسهام!","درجات المعنى! متوتر، خائف، مذعور. شجاع، جريء، لا يعرف الخوف. مسرور، سعيد، مبتهج جدًا!","اختر الكلمة الأدق؛ فهي تجعل كتابتك قوية!"],"voice":"Narrator: American English, warm male voice, speed 0.95."},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"RW-L05-U4-LS1-A1","type":"mcq","stage":"controlled","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct word.","instructions_ar":"اختر الكلمة الصحيحة.","items":[{"q":"The firefighters ___ the family from the burning building.","answer":"rescued","explanation":"Rescue.","explanation_ar":"أنقذوا.","options":["admired","inspired","demonstrated","rescued"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"A person you want to be like is your ___.","answer":"role model","explanation":"Role model.","explanation_ar":"قدوة.","options":["challenge","sacrifice","role model","integrity"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Telling the truth even when no one is watching shows ___.","answer":"integrity","explanation":"Integrity.","explanation_ar":"النزاهة.","options":["integrity","challenge","achievement","rescue"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"He won the prize but said, \"My team did the hard work.\" He is very ___.","answer":"humble","explanation":"Humble.","explanation_ar":"متواضع.","options":["humble","determined","terrified","exhausted"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Climbing the highest mountain in the region was a great ___.","answer":"achievement","explanation":"Achievement.","explanation_ar":"إنجاز.","options":["responsibility","integrity","sacrifice","achievement"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"The volunteer gave up her holiday to help sick children. She is ___.","answer":"selfless","explanation":"Selfless.","explanation_ar":"مُؤثِرة لغيرها.","options":["humble","selfless","fearless","bold"],"dok":2,"skill":"vocabulary","stage":"controlled"}]},{"id":"RW-L05-U4-LS1-A2","type":"mcq","stage":"guided","instructions":"Guided practice: Shades of meaning. Choose.","instructions_ar":"درجات المعنى: اختر.","items":[{"q":"Which order of fear words goes from WEAKEST to STRONGEST?","answer":"nervous → scared → terrified","explanation":"Weak → strong.","explanation_ar":"الترتيب الصحيح.","options":["nervous → scared → terrified","terrified → nervous → scared","scared → terrified → nervous","terrified → scared → nervous"],"dok":1,"skill":"shades of meaning","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which word is the STRONGEST?","answer":"thrilled","explanation":"Strength.","explanation_ar":"thrilled.","options":["glad","happy","okay","thrilled"],"dok":1,"skill":"shades of meaning","stage":"guided"},{"q":"*When the lights went out, little Lama screamed and hid under the table.* Which word fits BEST?","answer":"terrified","explanation":"Context: screamed and hid.","explanation_ar":"مذعورة.","options":["nervous","terrified","a bit worried","calm"],"dok":2,"skill":"shades of meaning","stage":"guided"},{"q":"*Before his speech, Sami's hands shook a little.* Which word fits BEST?","answer":"nervous","explanation":"Small fear.","explanation_ar":"متوتر.","options":["terrified","fearless","nervous","thrilled"],"dok":2,"skill":"shades of meaning","stage":"guided"},{"q":"After rescuing people all night, the team could hardly walk. They were ___.","answer":"exhausted","explanation":"Strong tiredness.","explanation_ar":"منهكين.","options":["a little tired","exhausted","sleepy","relaxed"],"dok":2,"skill":"shades of meaning","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which word for courage can sometimes sound a little RUDE?","answer":"bold","explanation":"Feeling of the word.","explanation_ar":"bold.","options":["brave","courageous","bold","heroic"],"dok":3,"skill":"connotation","stage":"guided"}]},{"id":"RW-L05-U4-LS1-A3","type":"gap_fill","stage":"freer","instructions":"Freer practice: Use the word bank.","instructions_ar":"استخدم بنك الكلمات.","items":[{"q":"The rescuers ________ great courage during the storm.","answer":"demonstrated","explanation":"Showed.","explanation_ar":"أظهروا.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Everyone can ________ to the school's charity drive.","answer":"contribute","explanation":"Help/give.","explanation_ar":"يسهم.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Our coach knows how to ________ us when we are tired.","answer":"motivate","explanation":"Make us want to try.","explanation_ar":"يحفّز.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Even when the math was difficult, she decided to ________.","answer":"persevere","explanation":"Keep trying.","explanation_ar":"تثابر.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Sami finally ________ his fear of thunderstorms.","answer":"overcame","explanation":"Past of overcome.","explanation_ar":"تغلّب على.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Looking after the class plants is our ________.","answer":"responsibility","explanation":"Duty.","explanation_ar":"مسؤوليتنا.","stage":"freer"}]},{"id":"RW-L05-U4-LS1-A4","type":"open","stage":"production","instructions":"Writing: Write with the new words.","instructions_ar":"اكتب باستخدام الكلمات الجديدة.","items":[{"q":"Write three sentences that show *nervous*, *scared* and *terrified* in different situations.","answer":"I felt nervous before my exam. I was scared when the dog barked. My sister was terrified during the loud storm.","explanation":"Shades.","explanation_ar":"درجات.","dok":2,"skill":"shades of meaning","stage":"production"},{"q":"Describe someone you admire using *integrity* or *selfless*.","answer":"My uncle is selfless; he spends every Friday helping at a charity kitchen.","explanation":"Describe.","explanation_ar":"صِف.","dok":2,"skill":"connect","stage":"production"},{"q":"What challenge have you overcome? How?","answer":"I overcame my fear of swimming by practicing every week with my cousin.","explanation":"Reflect.","explanation_ar":"تأمّل.","dok":2,"skill":"reflect","stage":"production"},{"q":"Do you think a hero must be famous? Why or why not?","answer":"No, because ordinary people like nurses and neighbors do brave and selfless things every day.","explanation":"Opinion.","explanation_ar":"رأي.","dok":3,"skill":"reasoning","stage":"production"}]}],"game":{"name":"Paint Strip Power","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["On this screen: answer the lesson questions as fast as you can.","In class: Shade slider: the child drags words onto a color strip from light to dark, then reads a situation and picks the word with the right strength. Correct choices light up a hero badge.","Teams get a word set and a paint strip.","They place the words from weakest to strongest.","The teacher reads a situation card; teams choose the best word from their strip.","Teams explain why their word is the most exact.","Correct order = 2 points; correct word for a situation = 1 point."],"data":[]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"Which word means *the ability to do something frightening*?","answer":"courage","explanation":"Courage.","explanation_ar":"شجاعة.","options":["integrity","achievement","challenge","courage"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary"},{"q":"What are *shades of meaning*?","answer":"similar words with different strengths","explanation":"Definition.","explanation_ar":"درجات المعنى.","options":["similar words with different strengths","words that rhyme","opposites","words in another language"],"dok":1,"skill":"shades of meaning"},{"q":"*She **persevered** and finally learned to swim.* *Persevered* means ___.","answer":"kept trying even when it was hard","explanation":"Persevere.","explanation_ar":"ثابرت.","options":["gave up quickly","forgot","kept trying even when it was hard","laughed"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary in context"},{"q":"Which word is WEAKER than *terrified*?","answer":"nervous","explanation":"Weaker.","explanation_ar":"nervous.","options":["nervous","horrified","petrified","panicked"],"dok":1,"skill":"shades of meaning"},{"q":"Which sentence about Sami and the storms is correct?","answer":"Sami overcame his fear of storms.","explanation":"Irregular past.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["Sami overcomed his fear of storms.","Sami overcome his fear of storms last night.","Sami overcoming his fear of storms yesterday.","Sami overcame his fear of storms."],"dok":2,"skill":"grammar"},{"q":"*The rescuer ran into the flood without stopping to think about danger.* Which word fits BEST?","answer":"fearless","explanation":"Strong courage.","explanation_ar":"لا يعرف الخوف.","options":["nervous","fearless","a bit brave","scared"],"dok":2,"skill":"shades of meaning"},{"q":"Which sentence uses *inspire* correctly?","answer":"Her story inspired me to study medicine.","explanation":"inspire + object + to.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["Her story inspired me to study medicine.","Her story inspired to me study medicine.","She inspired at me.","I inspired her story."],"dok":2,"skill":"grammar"},{"q":"Which word is the BEST choice? *I was ___ when I found a small scratch on my bike.*","answer":"a little upset","explanation":"Match strength to situation.","explanation_ar":"منزعج قليلًا.","options":["devastated","terrified","a little upset","heartbroken"],"dok":2,"skill":"shades of meaning"},{"q":"Why do writers choose EXACT words instead of *very very*?","answer":"Exact words give a clear, strong picture in fewer words.","explanation":"Word choice.","explanation_ar":"الكلمة الدقيقة أوضح وأقوى.","options":["Exact words are always longer.","Exact words rhyme.","Exact words give a clear, strong picture in fewer words.","Teachers don't like very."],"dok":3,"skill":"word choice"},{"q":"A nurse works on Eid day so that patients are cared for. Which word describes her BEST?","answer":"selfless","explanation":"Apply.","explanation_ar":"مُؤثِرة لغيرها.","options":["bold","selfless","terrified","thrilled"],"dok":3,"skill":"apply"}],"images":[{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V01","prompt":"Picture for the word 'courage': a child holding a flashlight in a storm"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V02","prompt":"Picture for the word 'rescue': rescuers helping a man into a truck"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V03","prompt":"Picture for the word 'sacrifice': a nurse working late at night"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V04","prompt":"Picture for the word 'integrity': a child returning a lost wallet"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V05","prompt":"Picture for the word 'determined': a runner pushing hard to the finish"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V06","prompt":"Picture for the word 'inspire': a girl looking up at a poster of an astronaut"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V07","prompt":"Picture for the word 'admire': a child smiling at a grandfather"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V08","prompt":"Picture for the word 'achievement': a trophy and a rocket"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V09","prompt":"Picture for the word 'challenge': a steep mountain path"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V10","prompt":"Picture for the word 'overcome': a child climbing over a wall"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V11","prompt":"Picture for the word 'role model': a child copying a teacher's kind action"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V12","prompt":"Picture for the word 'responsibility': an older child holding a younger child's hand"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V13","prompt":"Picture for the word 'humble': a person smiling shyly while others clap"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V14","prompt":"Picture for the word 'selfless': a volunteer handing out food"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V15","prompt":"Picture for the word 'demonstrate': a person showing something to a group"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V16","prompt":"Picture for the word 'contribute': hands putting coins in a box"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V17","prompt":"Picture for the word 'motivate': a coach cheering a runner"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V18","prompt":"Picture for the word 'persevere': a climber still climbing in the wind"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS1-01","prompt":"Everyday heroes and Sami with a flashlight."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS1-02","prompt":"Icons for hero words."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS1-03","prompt":"Paint strips showing shades of meaning."}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V01","script":"courage. It took courage to help in the storm."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V02","script":"rescue. The team rescued the old man."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V03","script":"sacrifice. Doctors make sacrifices to help patients."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V04","script":"integrity. A person with integrity tells the truth."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V05","script":"determined. She was determined to finish the race."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V06","script":"inspire. Her story inspired me to study science."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V07","script":"admire. I admire my grandfather's patience."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V08","script":"achievement. Going to space was a great achievement."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V09","script":"challenge. Learning a new language is a challenge."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V10","script":"overcome. Sami overcame his fear of storms."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V11","script":"role model. My teacher is my role model."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V12","script":"responsibility. Looking after my sister is my responsibility."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V13","script":"humble. The hero was humble and said, 'I just helped.'"},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V14","script":"selfless. The volunteer was selfless and worked all night."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V15","script":"demonstrate. He demonstrated great courage."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V16","script":"contribute. Everyone can contribute to a cleaner school."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V17","script":"motivate. My coach motivates me to practice."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS1-V18","script":"persevere. She persevered and finally passed the test."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS1-VID","script":"Not all heroes wear capes. Some carry flashlights, stethoscopes or school bags! Heroes show courage, integrity and responsibility. They are selfless and humble. They rescue, inspire and overcome challenges! We admire role models for their achievements and their sacrifices – and they motivate us to persevere and contribute! Shades of meaning! Nervous, scared, terrified. Brave, bold, fearless. Glad, happy, thrilled! Choose the most exact word – it makes your writing powerful!"}]},{"id":"RW-L05-U4-LS2","title":"The Night of the Storm","lesson_type":"close_reading","objectives":["read a realistic story of about 380 words about everyday courage","analyze how the author builds suspense (short sentences, sounds, time pressure, a problem that gets worse)","explain the theme with evidence from the dialogue and the ending"],"objectives_ar":["قراءة قصة واقعية من نحو 440 كلمة عن الشجاعة اليومية.","تحليل كيف يبني الكاتب التشويق.","شرح المغزى بالدليل من الحوار والنهاية."],"success_criteria":["I can find three ways the author makes the story exciting.","I can explain what the figurative language means (like a river, my lighthouse).","I can state the theme in a sentence and support it with a quotation."],"success_criteria_ar":["أستطيع إيجاد ثلاث طرق جعل بها الكاتب القصة مشوّقة.","أستطيع شرح معنى اللغة المجازية.","أستطيع صياغة المغزى في جملة ودعمه باقتباس."],"map_area":"Literary Text: Key Ideas and Details","vocabulary":[{"word":"hammer","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˈhæmər/","definition":"to hit something hard again and again","arabic":"يطرق بقوة","example":"Rain hammered on the windows.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS2-V01","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS2-V01","tier":"core"},{"word":"howl","pos":"verb","ipa":"/haʊl/","definition":"to make a long, loud, sad sound","arabic":"يعوي / يصفر","example":"The wind howled around the house.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS2-V02","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS2-V02","tier":"core"},{"word":"flashlight","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈflæʃˌlaɪt/","definition":"a small electric light you hold in your hand","arabic":"مصباح يدوي","example":"Sami switched on the flashlight.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS2-V03","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS2-V03","tier":"core"},{"word":"blink","pos":"verb","ipa":"/blɪŋk/","definition":"to go on and off quickly","arabic":"يومض","example":"A small light was blinking in the window.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS2-V04","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS2-V04","tier":"core"},{"word":"elderly","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈɛldərli/","definition":"old (a polite word for people)","arabic":"مسنّ","example":"Mr. Hamdan is our elderly neighbor.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS2-V05","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS2-V05","tier":"core"},{"word":"creep","pos":"verb","ipa":"/krip/","definition":"to move slowly and quietly (past: crept)","arabic":"يزحف / يتسلل","example":"Water was creeping under the door.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS2-V06","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS2-V06","tier":"core"},{"word":"suspense","pos":"noun","ipa":"/səˈspɛns/","definition":"the excited, worried feeling of waiting to find out what will happen","arabic":"التشويق","example":"The storm scene is full of suspense.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS2-V07","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS2-V07","tier":"core"}],"explanation":{"text":"**Suspense** is the worried, excited feeling of **waiting to find out what will happen**. Authors build it in several ways: a **problem that gets worse**, **time pressure** (help may not come in time), **strong sound and action words** (hammered, howled, crack), **short sentences** at exciting moments and **questions in the reader's mind**.\n\n**Figurative language** adds pictures and feelings: *water rushing down the street **like a river*** (simile) shows how much water there is; *You were my **lighthouse*** (metaphor) shows that Sami's light guided help to Mr. Hamdan.\n\nThe **theme** is often said by a wise character near the end and shown in the last lines. Look for it in **dialogue** and in how the main character **acts differently** at the end.","examples":["**Problem gets worse:** the storm → the lights go out → water in the street → an SOS signal.","**Short sentences:** *Lama screamed.* / *He just listened.*","**Sound words:** *Rain **hammered**… the wind **howled**… with a loud **crack**…*","**Time pressure:** *They might not find the right house.*","**Simile:** *water rushing down the street **like a river*** → there was a lot of fast water.","**Metaphor:** *\"You were my **lighthouse** last night.\"* → Sami's light guided the rescuers, like a lighthouse guides ships.","**Theme in dialogue:** *\"Courage doesn't mean you're not afraid… It means you do the right thing even when you are.\"*","**Theme in the ending:** *Sami didn't hide under his blanket. He just listened.* → his fear is smaller now.","**Theme sentence:** ***True courage means helping others even when you feel afraid.***"],"common_errors":["✗ Thinking Sami was not afraid. → ✓ He was afraid, but he acted anyway. (Read the evidence: 'his own voice was shaking'.)","✗ Taking 'You were my lighthouse' literally. → ✓ It is a metaphor: Sami guided help like a lighthouse. (Figurative, not real.)","✗ The theme is 'storms are dangerous'. → ✓ The theme is about courage and helping others. (Theme = lesson for life.)","✗ Sami go outside into the flood. → ✓ Sami stayed safely inside and signaled from the window. (Check the facts (and stay safe!).)","✗ The water was creeped under the door. → ✓ Water was creeping under the door. (Past continuous: was creeping.)","✗ Mother called to the emergency number. → ✓ Mother called the emergency number. (call + number (no **to**).)"],"arabic":"التشويق شعور القلق والحماس في انتظار ما سيحدث، ويبنيه الكاتب بمشكلة تتفاقم وضغط الوقت وكلمات الصوت والحركة القوية والجمل القصيرة.\n\nاللغة المجازية تضيف صورًا ومشاعر: «تجري كالنهر» تشبيه، و«كنتَ منارتي» استعارة تعني أن ضوء سامي أرشد المنقذين.\n\nالمغزى غالبًا تقوله شخصية حكيمة قرب النهاية، ويظهر في تغيّر تصرف البطل في السطور الأخيرة.\n\nتذكير بالسلامة: في السيول ابقَ في مكان آمن واتصل بالطوارئ، كما فعل سامي وأمه."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:25","narration":"Flash… crack… boom! Sami hates thunderstorms. But tonight, someone needs his help.","on_screen":"The Night of the Storm ⛈️","visual":"Lightning over a dark neighborhood; Sami under a blanket."},{"time":"00:25–02:10","narration":"Sami had always hated thunderstorms…","on_screen":"(story)","visual":"Animated story: the power cut, the flashlight, water rushing down the street, the SOS light, the phone call, Sami signaling from the window, the rescue truck, the morning visit."},{"time":"02:10–02:45","narration":"How does the author build suspense? A problem that gets worse, sound words, short sentences, time pressure!","on_screen":"Suspense builders ⏳","visual":"A tension meter rises with each event."},{"time":"02:45–03:15","narration":"\"You were my lighthouse.\" A metaphor! Sami's light guided help, like a lighthouse guides ships.","on_screen":"Figurative language 🗼","visual":"Sami's window turns into a lighthouse beam."},{"time":"03:15–03:30","narration":"Courage doesn't mean you're not afraid. It means doing the right thing anyway.","on_screen":"Theme 💡","visual":"Sami calmly listening to distant thunder."}],"captions_ar":["وميض… طقطقة… هدير! سامي يكره العواصف الرعدية، لكن الليلة يحتاج أحدٌ إلى مساعدته.","لطالما كره سامي العواصف الرعدية…","كيف يبني الكاتب التشويق؟ مشكلة تتفاقم، وكلمات صوتية، وجمل قصيرة، وضغط الوقت!","«كنتَ منارتي». استعارة! ضوء سامي أرشد المساعدة كما ترشد المنارة السفن.","الشجاعة لا تعني ألّا تخاف، بل أن تفعل الصواب رغم الخوف."],"voice":"Narrator: American English, dramatic but warm male storyteller, speed 0.95. A gentle elderly voice for Mr. Hamdan."},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"The Night of the Storm","body":"Sami had always hated thunderstorms. Every time the sky flashed, he pulled his blanket over his head and counted the seconds until the thunder came.\n\nThat winter night, the storm was the worst he had ever heard. Rain hammered on the windows, and the wind howled around the house. Father was working a night shift at the hospital, so only Sami, his mother and his little sister Lama were at home.\n\nSuddenly, with a loud crack, the lights went out. Lama screamed. Sami's heart jumped, but he found the flashlight in the kitchen drawer and switched it on. \"It's okay, Lama,\" he said, although his own voice was shaking.\n\nFrom the window, Sami could see water rushing down the street like a river. Then he noticed something strange. In the house across the road, a small light was blinking: three short flashes, three long ones, three short.\n\n\"Mom!\" Sami gasped. \"That's SOS! It's Mr. Hamdan's house!\"\n\nMr. Hamdan was their elderly neighbor. He lived alone and walked with a stick. Sami pictured him in the dark, with water creeping under his door.\n\nMother quickly called the emergency number. \"Help is coming,\" she said after the call, \"but the street is very dark. They might not find the right house.\"\n\nSami looked at the flashlight in his hand. He was still afraid of the storm, but he was more afraid for Mr. Hamdan. Staying safely inside, he stood at the window and flashed his light back across the street: I see you. Help is coming.\n\nTwenty minutes later, the headlights of a rescue truck appeared at the end of the road. Sami waved his flashlight in big circles and then pointed it straight at Mr. Hamdan's door. The rescuers splashed through the water, and soon they were helping the old man into the truck.\n\nThe next morning, the sun was shining. Mr. Hamdan, dry and safe, knocked on their door with a box of sweets.\n\n\"You were my lighthouse last night,\" he told Sami.\n\nSami smiled shyly. \"I was scared the whole time.\"\n\nMother put an arm around him. \"Courage doesn't mean you're not afraid,\" she said. \"It means you do the right thing even when you are.\"\n\nThat night, when the thunder rolled again, Sami didn't hide under his blanket. He just listened.","word_count":383,"audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS2-T1","id":"TXT-RW-L05-U4-LS2-1","genre":"narrative","role":"main","difficulty":"550L–750L","glossary":[{"word":"night shift","definition":"work that people do at night","arabic":"نوبة ليلية"},{"word":"SOS","definition":"an international signal that means 'Help!'","arabic":"إشارة استغاثة"},{"word":"lighthouse","definition":"a tall tower with a strong light that guides ships","arabic":"منارة"}]}],"activities":[{"id":"RW-L05-U4-LS2-A1","type":"mcq","stage":"controlled","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read the story. Choose the answer.","instructions_ar":"اقرأ القصة واختر الإجابة.","items":[{"q":"What did Sami usually do during thunderstorms?","answer":"He pulled his blanket over his head.","explanation":"Paragraph 1.","explanation_ar":"يغطي رأسه بالبطانية.","options":["He went outside to watch.","He called his friends.","He played football.","He pulled his blanket over his head."],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Where was Father on the night of the storm?","answer":"working a night shift at the hospital","explanation":"Paragraph 2.","explanation_ar":"في نوبة ليلية بالمستشفى.","options":["at Mr. Hamdan's house","working a night shift at the hospital","at the mosque","asleep upstairs"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"What did Sami see blinking in the house across the road?","answer":"an SOS signal: three short flashes, three long, three short","explanation":"Paragraph 4.","explanation_ar":"إشارة استغاثة.","options":["a television","a fire","an SOS signal: three short flashes, three long, three short","a birthday candle"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Who called the emergency number?","answer":"Mother","explanation":"Paragraph 7.","explanation_ar":"الأم.","options":["Mother","Sami","Lama","Mr. Hamdan"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"How did Sami help the rescuers find the right house?","answer":"He pointed his flashlight straight at Mr. Hamdan's door.","explanation":"Paragraph 9.","explanation_ar":"وجّه المصباح إلى باب السيد حمدان.","options":["He ran into the street to show them.","He pointed his flashlight straight at Mr. Hamdan's door.","He shouted the address.","He turned on all the lights."],"dok":2,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"What did Mr. Hamdan bring the next morning?","answer":"a box of sweets","explanation":"Paragraph 10.","explanation_ar":"علبة حلوى.","options":["a new flashlight","a lighthouse","an umbrella","a box of sweets"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"}]},{"id":"RW-L05-U4-LS2-A2","type":"mcq","stage":"guided","instructions":"Guided practice: Suspense, figurative language and theme. Choose.","instructions_ar":"التشويق واللغة المجازية والمغزى: اختر.","items":[{"q":"Which sentence uses SOUND words to build suspense?","answer":"Rain hammered on the windows, and the wind howled around the house.","explanation":"Sound words.","explanation_ar":"كلمات صوتية.","options":["The next morning, the sun was shining.","Rain hammered on the windows, and the wind howled around the house.","Sami smiled shyly.","Mr. Hamdan was their elderly neighbor."],"dok":2,"skill":"suspense","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which sentence adds TIME PRESSURE?","answer":"They might not find the right house.","explanation":"Time pressure.","explanation_ar":"ضغط الوقت.","options":["They might not find the right house.","Lama screamed.","He just listened.","Sami smiled shyly."],"dok":2,"skill":"suspense","stage":"guided"},{"q":"What does *water rushing down the street like a river* show?","answer":"There was a lot of fast-moving water.","explanation":"Simile.","explanation_ar":"مياه كثيرة سريعة.","options":["There was a real river in the street.","The street was dry.","Sami was swimming.","There was a lot of fast-moving water."],"dok":2,"skill":"figurative language","stage":"guided"},{"q":"What does Mr. Hamdan mean by *You were my lighthouse*?","answer":"Sami's light guided help to him, like a lighthouse guides ships.","explanation":"Metaphor.","explanation_ar":"ضوء سامي أرشد المساعدة.","options":["Sami lives in a lighthouse.","Sami's light guided help to him, like a lighthouse guides ships.","Sami is very tall.","Sami turned on all the street lights."],"dok":3,"skill":"figurative language","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which sentence BEST states the theme?","answer":"Courage means doing the right thing even when you are afraid.","explanation":"Theme.","explanation_ar":"الشجاعة فعل الصواب رغم الخوف.","options":["Storms happen in winter.","Flashlights are useful.","Courage means doing the right thing even when you are afraid.","Neighbors bring sweets."],"dok":2,"skill":"theme","stage":"guided"},{"q":"How does the LAST line show that Sami has changed?","answer":"He no longer hides from thunder; he just listens.","explanation":"Ending.","explanation_ar":"لم يعد يختبئ من الرعد.","options":["He no longer hides from thunder; he just listens.","He still hides under his blanket.","He goes out into the storm.","He forgets about Mr. Hamdan."],"dok":3,"skill":"character change","stage":"guided"}]},{"id":"RW-L05-U4-LS2-A3","type":"highlight","stage":"freer","instructions":"Find the evidence: Find the evidence.","instructions_ar":"ابحث عن الدليل.","items":[{"q":"Underline the sentence that shows Sami was afraid but still acted.","answer":"He was still afraid of the storm, but he was more afraid for Mr. Hamdan.","explanation":"Motivation.","explanation_ar":"الدافع.","evidence":"He was still afraid of the storm, but he was more afraid for Mr. Hamdan.","text_id":"TXT-RW-L05-U4-LS2-1","dok":2,"skill":"evidence","stage":"freer","sentences":["Sami had always hated thunderstorms.","Every time the sky flashed, he pulled his blanket over his head and counted the seconds until the thunder came.","That winter night, the storm was the worst he had ever heard.","Rain hammered on the windows, and the wind howled around the house.","Father was working a night shift at the hospital, so only Sami, his mother and his little sister Lama were at home.","Suddenly, with a loud crack, the lights went out.","Lama screamed.","Sami's heart jumped, but he found the flashlight in the kitchen drawer and switched it on.","\"It's okay, Lama,\" he said, although his own voice was shaking.","From the window, Sami could see water rushing down the street like a river.","Then he noticed something strange.","In the house across the road, a small light was blinking: three short flashes, three long ones, three short.","\"Mom!\"","Sami gasped.","\"That's SOS!","It's Mr.","Hamdan's house!\"","Mr.","Hamdan was their elderly neighbor.","He lived alone and walked with a stick.","Sami pictured him in the dark, with water creeping under his door.","Mother quickly called the emergency number.","\"Help is coming,\" she said after the call, \"but the street is very dark.","They might not find the right house.\"","Sami looked at the flashlight in his hand.","He was still afraid of the storm, but he was more afraid for Mr.","Hamdan.","Staying safely inside, he stood at the window and flashed his light back across the street: I see you.","Help is coming.","Twenty minutes later, the headlights of a rescue truck appeared at the end of the road.","Sami waved his flashlight in big circles and then pointed it straight at Mr.","Hamdan's door.","The rescuers splashed through the water, and soon they were helping the old man into the truck.","The next morning, the sun was shining.","Mr.","Hamdan, dry and safe, knocked on their door with a box of sweets.","\"You were my lighthouse last night,\" he told Sami.","Sami smiled shyly.","\"I was scared the whole time.\"","Mother put an arm around him.","\"Courage doesn't mean you're not afraid,\" she said.","\"It means you do the right thing even when you are.\"","That night, when the thunder rolled again, Sami didn't hide under his blanket.","He just listened."]},{"q":"Underline the words that show Sami's voice gave away his fear.","answer":"although his own voice was shaking","explanation":"Evidence of fear.","explanation_ar":"دليل الخوف.","evidence":"although his own voice was shaking","text_id":"TXT-RW-L05-U4-LS2-1","dok":1,"skill":"evidence","stage":"freer","sentences":["Sami had always hated thunderstorms.","Every time the sky flashed, he pulled his blanket over his head and counted the seconds until the thunder came.","That winter night, the storm was the worst he had ever heard.","Rain hammered on the windows, and the wind howled around the house.","Father was working a night shift at the hospital, so only Sami, his mother and his little sister Lama were at home.","Suddenly, with a loud crack, the lights went out.","Lama screamed.","Sami's heart jumped, but he found the flashlight in the kitchen drawer and switched it on.","\"It's okay, Lama,\" he said, although his own voice was shaking.","From the window, Sami could see water rushing down the street like a river.","Then he noticed something strange.","In the house across the road, a small light was blinking: three short flashes, three long ones, three short.","\"Mom!\"","Sami gasped.","\"That's SOS!","It's Mr.","Hamdan's house!\"","Mr.","Hamdan was their elderly neighbor.","He lived alone and walked with a stick.","Sami pictured him in the dark, with water creeping under his door.","Mother quickly called the emergency number.","\"Help is coming,\" she said after the call, \"but the street is very dark.","They might not find the right house.\"","Sami looked at the flashlight in his hand.","He was still afraid of the storm, but he was more afraid for Mr.","Hamdan.","Staying safely inside, he stood at the window and flashed his light back across the street: I see you.","Help is coming.","Twenty minutes later, the headlights of a rescue truck appeared at the end of the road.","Sami waved his flashlight in big circles and then pointed it straight at Mr.","Hamdan's door.","The rescuers splashed through the water, and soon they were helping the old man into the truck.","The next morning, the sun was shining.","Mr.","Hamdan, dry and safe, knocked on their door with a box of sweets.","\"You were my lighthouse last night,\" he told Sami.","Sami smiled shyly.","\"I was scared the whole time.\"","Mother put an arm around him.","\"Courage doesn't mean you're not afraid,\" she said.","\"It means you do the right thing even when you are.\"","That night, when the thunder rolled again, Sami didn't hide under his blanket.","He just listened."]},{"q":"Why does the author tell us that Mr. Hamdan *lived alone and walked with a stick*?","answer":"to show he was in real danger and needed help","explanation":"Author's craft.","explanation_ar":"ليُظهر أنه في خطر حقيقي.","options":["to describe his house","to make the story funny","to show he was a rescuer","to show he was in real danger and needed help"],"dok":2,"skill":"author's craft","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Why is it important that Sami stayed *safely inside*?","answer":"It shows a safe and smart way to help in a flood.","explanation":"Safety.","explanation_ar":"طريقة آمنة للمساعدة.","options":["Because he was lazy.","Because the door was locked.","It shows a safe and smart way to help in a flood.","Because he wanted to sleep."],"dok":2,"skill":"inference","stage":"freer"}]},{"id":"RW-L05-U4-LS2-A4","type":"open","stage":"production","instructions":"Writing: Explain and respond.","instructions_ar":"اشرح واستجب.","items":[{"q":"Name two ways the author builds suspense. Give an example of each.","answer":"Sound words: 'the wind howled'. Time pressure: 'They might not find the right house.'","explanation":"Two techniques.","explanation_ar":"أسلوبان.","dok":2,"skill":"suspense","stage":"production"},{"q":"Explain the metaphor *You were my lighthouse* in your own words.","answer":"Sami's flashlight showed the rescuers where to go, just as a lighthouse shows ships the way in the dark.","explanation":"Metaphor.","explanation_ar":"استعارة.","dok":3,"skill":"figurative language","stage":"production"},{"q":"Write the theme of the story and support it with a quotation.","answer":"Courage means doing the right thing even when you are afraid: 'It means you do the right thing even when you are.'","explanation":"Theme + quote.","explanation_ar":"المغزى + اقتباس.","dok":3,"skill":"theme","stage":"production"},{"q":"Was Sami a hero? Why or why not?","answer":"Yes, because he overcame his fear and helped save his neighbor in a safe and clever way.","explanation":"Opinion + reason.","explanation_ar":"رأي + سبب.","dok":3,"skill":"evaluate","stage":"production"}]},{"id":"RW-L05-U4-LS2-TR-1","type":"timed_reading","instructions":"Timed reading: Read \"The Night of the Storm\" aloud or silently. Try to finish in the time.","instructions_ar":"اقرأ النص وحاول أن تنهيه في الوقت المحدد.","items":[{"q":"Read “The Night of the Storm”.","answer":"383 words","title":"The Night of the Storm","body":"Sami had always hated thunderstorms. Every time the sky flashed, he pulled his blanket over his head and counted the seconds until the thunder came.\n\nThat winter night, the storm was the worst he had ever heard. Rain hammered on the windows, and the wind howled around the house. Father was working a night shift at the hospital, so only Sami, his mother and his little sister Lama were at home.\n\nSuddenly, with a loud crack, the lights went out. Lama screamed. Sami's heart jumped, but he found the flashlight in the kitchen drawer and switched it on. \"It's okay, Lama,\" he said, although his own voice was shaking.\n\nFrom the window, Sami could see water rushing down the street like a river. Then he noticed something strange. In the house across the road, a small light was blinking: three short flashes, three long ones, three short.\n\n\"Mom!\" Sami gasped. \"That's SOS! It's Mr. Hamdan's house!\"\n\nMr. Hamdan was their elderly neighbor. He lived alone and walked with a stick. Sami pictured him in the dark, with water creeping under his door.\n\nMother quickly called the emergency number. \"Help is coming,\" she said after the call, \"but the street is very dark. They might not find the right house.\"\n\nSami looked at the flashlight in his hand. He was still afraid of the storm, but he was more afraid for Mr. Hamdan. Staying safely inside, he stood at the window and flashed his light back across the street: I see you. Help is coming.\n\nTwenty minutes later, the headlights of a rescue truck appeared at the end of the road. Sami waved his flashlight in big circles and then pointed it straight at Mr. Hamdan's door. The rescuers splashed through the water, and soon they were helping the old man into the truck.\n\nThe next morning, the sun was shining. Mr. Hamdan, dry and safe, knocked on their door with a box of sweets.\n\n\"You were my lighthouse last night,\" he told Sami.\n\nSami smiled shyly. \"I was scared the whole time.\"\n\nMother put an arm around him. \"Courage doesn't mean you're not afraid,\" she said. \"It means you do the right thing even when you are.\"\n\nThat night, when the thunder rolled again, Sami didn't hide under his blanket. He just listened.","words":383,"limit":244}],"time_limit_sec":244}],"game":{"name":"Suspense Meter","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["On this screen: answer the lesson questions as fast as you can.","In class: Tension meter: sentences appear one by one; the child slides the meter to show the suspense level and taps the technique used. Correct answers make the storm animation build, then calm at the end.","A team draws a sentence strip and reads it dramatically.","They place it on the suspense meter (1–10).","They name the technique or figurative language used.","Other teams agree or challenge with evidence.","Correct technique = 2 points; good dramatic reading = 1 bonus point."],"data":[]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"What is *suspense*?","answer":"the worried, excited feeling of waiting to find out what happens","explanation":"Suspense.","explanation_ar":"التشويق.","options":["the end of a story","a list of characters","a kind of storm","the worried, excited feeling of waiting to find out what happens"],"dok":1,"skill":"suspense"},{"q":"What does *SOS* mean?","answer":"Help!","explanation":"Glossary.","explanation_ar":"النجدة!","options":["Hello!","Help!","Goodbye!","Good night!"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary"},{"q":"*Water was **creeping** under his door.* *Creeping* means ___.","answer":"moving slowly and quietly","explanation":"Creep.","explanation_ar":"يتسلل ببطء.","options":["moving slowly and quietly","jumping high","drying fast","freezing"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary in context"},{"q":"Which is a METAPHOR from the story?","answer":"You were my lighthouse.","explanation":"Metaphor.","explanation_ar":"استعارة.","options":["water rushing like a river","The lights went out.","You were my lighthouse.","Lama screamed."],"dok":2,"skill":"figurative language"},{"q":"Which sentence about the phone call is correct?","answer":"Mother called the emergency number.","explanation":"call + number.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["Mother called the emergency number.","Mother called to the emergency number.","Mother calling the emergency number.","Mother call the emergency number last night."],"dok":2,"skill":"grammar"},{"q":"Why was Sami's flashlight so important?","answer":"The street was dark, and the rescuers needed to find the right house.","explanation":"Cause → effect.","explanation_ar":"لإرشاد المنقذين في الظلام.","options":["It played music.","It warmed the house.","The street was dark, and the rescuers needed to find the right house.","It stopped the rain."],"dok":2,"skill":"cause and effect"},{"q":"What was Sami's MOTIVATION for signaling to Mr. Hamdan?","answer":"He was worried about his elderly neighbor.","explanation":"Motivation.","explanation_ar":"قلقه على جاره.","options":["He wanted a box of sweets.","He was worried about his elderly neighbor.","He liked playing with lights.","His father told him to."],"dok":2,"skill":"motivation"},{"q":"Which detail shows the storm was very strong?","answer":"Water was rushing down the street like a river.","explanation":"Evidence.","explanation_ar":"المياه كالنهر.","options":["Mother hugged Sami.","Mr. Hamdan brought sweets.","Father worked at the hospital.","Water was rushing down the street like a river."],"dok":2,"skill":"evidence"},{"q":"What does Mother's advice teach the READER?","answer":"Being brave is about acting rightly, not about having no fear.","explanation":"Theme.","explanation_ar":"الشجاعة عمل الصواب.","options":["Being brave is about acting rightly, not about having no fear.","Never be afraid of anything.","Storms are fun.","Only adults can be brave."],"dok":3,"skill":"theme"},{"q":"Why does the author end with short sentences: *He just listened.*?","answer":"to show calmly and simply how much Sami has changed","explanation":"Author's craft.","explanation_ar":"ليُظهر التغيّر بهدوء.","options":["because the author ran out of words","to show calmly and simply how much Sami has changed","to start a new problem","to describe the weather"],"dok":3,"skill":"author's craft"}],"images":[{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS2-V01","prompt":"Picture for the word 'hammer': heavy rain hitting a window"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS2-V02","prompt":"Picture for the word 'howl': trees bending in a strong wind"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS2-V03","prompt":"Picture for the word 'flashlight': a hand holding a flashlight"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS2-V04","prompt":"Picture for the word 'blink': a light turning on and off"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS2-V05","prompt":"Picture for the word 'elderly': an old man with a walking stick"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS2-V06","prompt":"Picture for the word 'creep': water slowly coming under a door"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS2-V07","prompt":"Picture for the word 'suspense': a reader holding a book tightly"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS2-01","prompt":"Sami signaling with a flashlight from his window during a storm."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS2-02","prompt":"Rescuers helping an elderly neighbor during a flood."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS2-03","prompt":"A tension graph of the story."}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS2-V01","script":"hammer. Rain hammered on the windows."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS2-V02","script":"howl. The wind howled around the house."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS2-V03","script":"flashlight. Sami switched on the flashlight."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS2-V04","script":"blink. A small light was blinking in the window."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS2-V05","script":"elderly. Mr. Hamdan is our elderly neighbor."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS2-V06","script":"creep. Water was creeping under the door."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS2-V07","script":"suspense. The storm scene is full of suspense."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS2-T1","script":"Sami had always hated thunderstorms. Every time the sky flashed, he pulled his blanket over his head and counted the seconds until the thunder came. That winter night, the storm was the worst he had ever heard. Rain hammered on the windows, and the wind howled around the house. Father was working a night shift at the hospital, so only Sami, his mother and his little sister Lama were at home. Suddenly, with a loud crack, the lights went out. Lama screamed. Sami's heart jumped, but he found the flashlight in the kitchen drawer and switched it on. \"It's okay, Lama,\" he said, although his own voice was shaking. From the window, Sami could see water rushing down the street like a river. Then he noticed something strange. In the house across the road, a small light was blinking: three short flashes, three long ones, three short. \"Mom!\" Sami gasped. \"That's SOS! It's Mr. Hamdan's house!\" Mr. Hamdan was their elderly neighbor. He lived alone and walked with a stick. Sami pictured him in the dark, with water creeping under his door. Mother quickly called the emergency number. \"Help is coming,\" she said after the call, \"but the street is very dark. They might not find the right house.\" Sami looked at the flashlight in his hand. He was still afraid of the storm, but he was more afraid for Mr. Hamdan. Staying safely inside, he stood at the window and flashed his light back across the street: I see you. Help is coming. Twenty minutes later, the headlights of a rescue truck appeared at the end of the road. Sami waved his flashlight in big circles and then pointed it straight at Mr. Hamdan's door. The rescuers splashed through the water, and soon they were helping the old man into the truck. The next morning, the sun was shining. Mr. Hamdan, dry and safe, knocked on their door with a box of sweets. \"You were my lighthouse last night,\" he told Sami. Sami smiled shyly. \"I was scared the whole time.\" Mother put an arm around him. \"Courage doesn't mean you're not afraid,\" she said. \"It means you do the right thing even when you are.\" That night, when the thunder rolled again, Sami didn't hide under his blanket. He just listened."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS2-VID","script":"Flash… crack… boom! Sami hates thunderstorms. But tonight, someone needs his help. Sami had always hated thunderstorms… How does the author build suspense? A problem that gets worse, sound words, short sentences, time pressure! \"You were my lighthouse.\" A metaphor! Sami's light guided help, like a lighthouse guides ships. Courage doesn't mean you're not afraid. It means doing the right thing anyway."}]},{"id":"RW-L05-U4-LS3","title":"Character motivation and change: \"A Letter to My Hero\"","lesson_type":"strategy_paired_text","objectives":["explain a character's or writer's motivation: the reasons behind their actions and choices","describe how a character changes from the beginning to the end and what causes the change","compare motivation and change in a story and a letter"],"objectives_ar":["شرح دوافع الشخصية أو الكاتب: أسباب أفعالها وقراراتها.","وصف كيف تتغير الشخصية من البداية إلى النهاية وما يسبب التغيّر.","مقارنة الدوافع والتغيّر في قصة ورسالة."],"success_criteria":["I can say WHY a character acts, using clues from thoughts, words and actions.","I can describe a character at the start and at the end, with evidence.","I can explain what caused the change."],"success_criteria_ar":["أستطيع قول لماذا تتصرف الشخصية بأدلة من أفكارها وأقوالها وأفعالها.","أستطيع وصف الشخصية في البداية والنهاية بالدليل.","أستطيع شرح سبب التغيّر."],"map_area":"Informational Text: Key Ideas and Details","vocabulary":[{"word":"astronaut","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈæstrəˌnɔt/","definition":"a person who travels into space","arabic":"رائد / رائدة فضاء","example":"She became the first Saudi woman astronaut.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS3-V01","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS3-V01","tier":"core"},{"word":"launch","pos":"noun / verb","ipa":"/lɔntʃ/","definition":"the moment a rocket goes up; to send a rocket up","arabic":"إطلاق / يُطلق","example":"We watched the launch on a big screen.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS3-V02","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS3-V02","tier":"core"},{"word":"research","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈrisɝtʃ/","definition":"careful study to discover new facts","arabic":"بحث علمي","example":"She did research on cells.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS3-V03","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS3-V03","tier":"core"},{"word":"risky","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈrɪski/","definition":"possibly dangerous","arabic":"محفوف بالمخاطر","example":"Traveling to space is risky.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS3-V04","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS3-V04","tier":"core"},{"word":"motivation","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌmoʊtəˈveɪʃən/","definition":"the reason why someone does something","arabic":"الدافع","example":"Sami's motivation was to help his neighbor.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS3-V05","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS3-V05","tier":"core"},{"word":"respect","pos":"noun","ipa":"/rɪˈspɛkt/","definition":"a feeling that someone is good and important","arabic":"احترام","example":"She signed the letter 'With great respect'.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS3-V06","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS3-V06","tier":"core"},{"word":"dream","pos":"noun / verb","ipa":"/drim/","definition":"something you very much want to do or be","arabic":"حلم / يحلم","example":"Our dreams can reach the stars.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS3-V07","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS3-V07","tier":"core"}],"explanation":{"text":"**Motivation** is the **reason** a character does something. It comes from **inside** (feelings, worries, hopes) or from **outside** (another person, an event). Find it in the character's **thoughts**, **words** and **actions**: *He was more afraid for Mr. Hamdan.*\n\nMany characters **change** during a story. Compare the character **at the beginning** and **at the end**, then find **what caused** the change (an event, a person, a lesson). Use the frame: ***At first, … . After …, … . By the end, … .***\n\nReal writers have motivations too. In a letter, the writer explains **why** she admires someone and **how** that person has **changed** her own ideas or dreams.","examples":["**Sami at the start:** *Sami had always hated thunderstorms… pulled his blanket over his head.* → fearful.","**Event:** the SOS signal from Mr. Hamdan's house.","**Sami's motivation:** *He was still afraid of the storm, but he was more afraid for Mr. Hamdan.* → caring for his neighbor.","**Sami at the end:** *Sami didn't hide under his blanket. He just listened.* → braver and calmer.","**Cause of change:** helping someone in danger showed him he could be brave even when afraid.","**Layla's motivation for writing:** *I am writing to tell you that you are my hero.* → admiration and thanks.","**Layla before:** *I only wanted to be an artist.* → **Layla after:** *Now I want to be an artist and a scientist.*","**Cause of Layla's change:** watching her hero go to space and do experiments for students.","**Compare:** both changed because of a **brave action** – Sami's own, and Layla's hero's."],"common_errors":["✗ Giving the action but not the reason. → ✓ Add because…: He signaled because he was worried about Mr. Hamdan. (Motivation = why.)","✗ Describing only the end. → ✓ Compare the start AND the end. (Change needs two points.)","✗ Guessing a motivation with no evidence. → ✓ Quote the thought, word or action. (Evidence!)","✗ Layla want to be a scientist now. → ✓ Layla wants to be a scientist now. (She → **wants**.)","✗ Sami was afraid but he help. → ✓ Sami was afraid, but he helped. (Past tense + comma before **but**.)","✗ The first Saudi woman go to space. → ✓ The first Saudi woman went to space. (Past tense: **went**.)"],"arabic":"الدافع هو سبب تصرف الشخصية، وقد يكون داخليًا (مشاعر ومخاوف وآمال) أو خارجيًا (شخص أو حدث)، ونجده في أفكارها وأقوالها وأفعالها.\n\nكثير من الشخصيات تتغير: قارن الشخصية في البداية والنهاية، وجِد سبب التغيّر، واستخدم: At first … After … By the end …\n\nللكُتّاب الحقيقيين دوافع أيضًا؛ ففي الرسالة تشرح الكاتبة لماذا تُعجب بشخص وكيف غيّر أحلامها.\n\nريانة برناوي أول امرأة سعودية تصعد إلى الفضاء (مايو 2023)، وهي باحثة في علوم الخلايا."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:25","narration":"10… 9… 8… A rocket is about to launch – and a girl in Taif is about to change her dream!","on_screen":"A Letter to My Hero 🚀✉️","visual":"Students in a school hall watch a rocket launch on a big screen."},{"time":"00:25–01:40","narration":"Dear Ms. Rayyanah Barnawi, My name is Layla…","on_screen":"(letter)","visual":"Layla writing at her desk; scenes of a laboratory, a rocket, the space station and students doing an experiment."},{"time":"01:40–02:25","narration":"Motivation = WHY a character acts. Sami helped because he was worried about his neighbor.","on_screen":"Motivation 💭","visual":"A thought bubble over Sami: 'He needs help!'"},{"time":"02:25–03:05","narration":"Change: At first … After … By the end … Sami became braver; Layla's dream grew bigger!","on_screen":"Before → Event → After","visual":"Two before-and-after pictures of Sami and Layla."},{"time":"03:05–03:30","narration":"Heroes inspire us to change. Who inspires YOU?","on_screen":"Who inspires you? 🌟","visual":"Layla paints planets in her sketchbook."}],"captions_ar":["10… 9… 8… صاروخ على وشك الانطلاق، وفتاة في الطائف على وشك أن يتغير حلمها!","عزيزتي الأستاذة ريانة برناوي، اسمي ليلى…","الدافع هو سبب تصرف الشخصية: ساعد سامي لأنه قلق على جاره.","التغيّر: في البداية… بعد… في النهاية… أصبح سامي أشجع، وكبر حلم ليلى!","الأبطال يلهموننا لنتغير. من يلهمك أنت؟"],"voice":"Narrator: American English, warm female voice, speed 0.95. Layla reads her letter with feeling."},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"A Letter to My Hero","body":"Dear Ms. Rayyanah Barnawi,\n\nMy name is Layla, and I am a student in Taif. I am writing to tell you that you are my hero.\n\nIn May 2023, you became the first Saudi woman to travel to space. My whole class watched the launch on the big screen in the school hall. When the rocket lifted off, we cheered so loudly that the principal came to see what was happening!\n\nI admire you for three reasons. First, you were determined. Before you became an astronaut, you spent many years studying and doing research on cells in laboratories, and you did not give up when the work was hard. Second, you showed great courage. Traveling to the International Space Station is risky, but you went to help science. Third, you remembered children like me. From space, you did simple science experiments with students across Saudi Arabia to inspire us.\n\nBefore your journey, I only wanted to be an artist. Now I want to be an artist and a scientist. I want to paint the planets and study them too!\n\nCould you tell me what Earth looked like from space? Were you afraid during the launch?\n\nThank you for showing girls like me that our dreams can reach the stars.\n\nWith great respect,\n\nLayla","word_count":213,"audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS3-T1","id":"TXT-RW-L05-U4-LS3-1","genre":"letter/email","role":"paired","difficulty":"550L–750L","glossary":[{"word":"astronaut","definition":"a person who travels into space","arabic":"رائد / رائدة فضاء"},{"word":"launch","definition":"the moment when a rocket goes up into the sky","arabic":"الإطلاق"},{"word":"International Space Station","definition":"a large laboratory that goes around the Earth where astronauts live and work","arabic":"محطة الفضاء الدولية"}]}],"activities":[{"id":"RW-L05-U4-LS3-A1","type":"mcq","stage":"controlled","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read Layla's letter. Choose the answer.","instructions_ar":"اقرأ رسالة ليلى واختر الإجابة.","items":[{"q":"Who is Layla's letter to?","answer":"Ms. Rayyanah Barnawi","explanation":"Greeting.","explanation_ar":"ريانة برناوي.","options":["her art teacher","her grandmother","Ms. Rayyanah Barnawi","Mr. Hamdan"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","text_id":"TXT-RW-L05-U4-LS3-1","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"What did Rayyanah Barnawi do in May 2023?","answer":"She became the first Saudi woman to travel to space.","explanation":"Paragraph 2.","explanation_ar":"أول سعودية تسافر إلى الفضاء.","options":["She became the first Saudi woman to travel to space.","She opened a school.","She painted the planets.","She built a rocket in Taif."],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Where did Layla's class watch the launch?","answer":"on the big screen in the school hall","explanation":"Paragraph 2.","explanation_ar":"على الشاشة الكبيرة في قاعة المدرسة.","options":["at the space station","at the airport","on the big screen in the school hall","on the radio"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"What did Rayyanah Barnawi study in laboratories before going to space?","answer":"cells","explanation":"Paragraph 3.","explanation_ar":"الخلايا.","options":["rocks","stars","sea animals","cells"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"How did she remember children from space?","answer":"She did simple science experiments with students across Saudi Arabia.","explanation":"Paragraph 3.","explanation_ar":"أجرت تجارب علمية مع الطلاب.","options":["She sent them toys.","She visited every school.","She wrote them a book.","She did simple science experiments with students across Saudi Arabia."],"dok":2,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"What two questions does Layla ask?","answer":"What Earth looked like from space and whether she was afraid during the launch","explanation":"Paragraph 5.","explanation_ar":"سؤالان عن الأرض والخوف.","options":["How old she is and where she lives","What Earth looked like from space and whether she was afraid during the launch","What she ate and what she wore","How fast the rocket was and how big it was"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"}]},{"id":"RW-L05-U4-LS3-A2","type":"mcq","stage":"guided","instructions":"Guided practice: Motivation and change. Choose.","instructions_ar":"الدافع والتغيّر: اختر.","items":[{"q":"What is Layla's MOTIVATION for writing the letter?","answer":"to tell her hero how much she admires her and to thank her","explanation":"Motivation.","explanation_ar":"الإعجاب والشكر.","options":["to ask for money","to tell her hero how much she admires her and to thank her","to complain about school","to invite her to a party"],"dok":1,"skill":"motivation","stage":"guided"},{"q":"How does Layla's dream CHANGE?","answer":"from only an artist to an artist and a scientist","explanation":"Change.","explanation_ar":"من فنانة إلى فنانة وعالمة.","options":["from a scientist to a doctor","from an astronaut to a teacher","It doesn't change.","from only an artist to an artist and a scientist"],"dok":1,"skill":"character change","stage":"guided"},{"q":"What CAUSED Layla's change?","answer":"watching her hero go to space and do experiments for students","explanation":"Cause of change.","explanation_ar":"مشاهدة بطلتها.","options":["watching her hero go to space and do experiments for students","a bad grade in art","a trip to the moon","a new paint set"],"dok":2,"skill":"character change","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which sentence shows Sami's MOTIVATION in *The Night of the Storm*?","answer":"He was still afraid of the storm, but he was more afraid for Mr. Hamdan.","explanation":"Motivation.","explanation_ar":"دافع سامي.","options":["He was still afraid of the storm, but he was more afraid for Mr. Hamdan.","The next morning, the sun was shining.","Rain hammered on the windows.","Father was working a night shift."],"dok":2,"skill":"motivation","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which frame BEST describes Sami's change?","answer":"At first, Sami hid from storms. After he helped Mr. Hamdan, he learned he could be brave. By the end, he just listened to the thunder.","explanation":"Change frame.","explanation_ar":"إطار التغيّر.","options":["Sami likes flashlights.","At first, Sami was brave. By the end, he was scared.","Sami never changed.","At first, Sami hid from storms. After he helped Mr. Hamdan, he learned he could be brave. By the end, he just listened to the thunder."],"dok":3,"skill":"character change","stage":"guided"},{"q":"How are Sami's and Layla's changes ALIKE?","answer":"Both changed because of a brave action – Sami's own and Layla's hero's.","explanation":"Compare texts.","explanation_ar":"كلاهما تغيّر بسبب عمل شجاع.","options":["Both went to space.","Both became artists.","Both changed because of a brave action – Sami's own and Layla's hero's.","Both were afraid of storms."],"dok":3,"skill":"compare texts","stage":"guided"}]},{"id":"RW-L05-U4-LS3-A3","type":"organizer","stage":"freer","instructions":"Organizer: Complete the Motivation & Change Map.","instructions_ar":"أكمل خريطة الدافع والتغيّر.","items":[{"q":"At first – describe Sami and Layla at the start, with evidence.","answer":"Sami hated storms and 'pulled his blanket over his head'. Layla 'only wanted to be an artist'.","explanation":"Start.","explanation_ar":"البداية.","dok":1,"skill":"character change","stage":"freer"},{"q":"The event or person that made a difference for each.","answer":"Sami: the SOS light from Mr. Hamdan's house. Layla: watching Rayyanah Barnawi travel to space.","explanation":"Event.","explanation_ar":"الحدث.","dok":2,"skill":"character change","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Motivation – why does each one act?","answer":"Sami acts because he is worried about his elderly neighbor. Layla writes because she admires her hero and wants to thank her.","explanation":"Motivation.","explanation_ar":"الدافع.","dok":2,"skill":"motivation","stage":"freer"},{"q":"By the end – how has each one changed? Evidence?","answer":"Sami no longer hides: 'He just listened.' Layla now wants to be 'an artist and a scientist'.","explanation":"End.","explanation_ar":"النهاية.","dok":2,"skill":"character change","stage":"freer"}]},{"id":"RW-L05-U4-LS3-A4","type":"open","stage":"production","instructions":"Writing: Explain motivation and change.","instructions_ar":"اشرح الدافع والتغيّر.","items":[{"q":"Write Sami's change with the frame *At first … After … By the end …*","answer":"At first, Sami hid from thunderstorms. After he helped rescue Mr. Hamdan, he realized he could be brave. By the end, he calmly listened to the thunder.","explanation":"Change frame.","explanation_ar":"إطار التغيّر.","dok":2,"skill":"character change","stage":"production"},{"q":"Why do you think Layla asks *Were you afraid during the launch?*","answer":"Maybe she wants to know if heroes feel fear too, like Sami did.","explanation":"Inference.","explanation_ar":"استنتاج.","dok":3,"skill":"inference","stage":"production"},{"q":"What qualities do Sami and Rayyanah Barnawi share? Give evidence for each.","answer":"Both showed courage: Sami helped in the storm even though he was scared, and Barnawi traveled to space even though it was risky.","explanation":"Compare.","explanation_ar":"قارن.","dok":3,"skill":"compare texts","stage":"production"},{"q":"Who has inspired YOU to change a dream or a habit? How?","answer":"My cousin, who is a nurse, inspired me to learn first aid.","explanation":"Connect.","explanation_ar":"ربط.","dok":2,"skill":"connect","stage":"production"}]},{"id":"RW-L05-U4-LS3-TR-1","type":"timed_reading","instructions":"Timed reading: Read \"A Letter to My Hero\" aloud or silently. Try to finish in the time.","instructions_ar":"اقرأ النص وحاول أن تنهيه في الوقت المحدد.","items":[{"q":"Read “A Letter to My Hero”.","answer":"213 words","title":"A Letter to My Hero","body":"Dear Ms. Rayyanah Barnawi,\n\nMy name is Layla, and I am a student in Taif. I am writing to tell you that you are my hero.\n\nIn May 2023, you became the first Saudi woman to travel to space. My whole class watched the launch on the big screen in the school hall. When the rocket lifted off, we cheered so loudly that the principal came to see what was happening!\n\nI admire you for three reasons. First, you were determined. Before you became an astronaut, you spent many years studying and doing research on cells in laboratories, and you did not give up when the work was hard. Second, you showed great courage. Traveling to the International Space Station is risky, but you went to help science. Third, you remembered children like me. From space, you did simple science experiments with students across Saudi Arabia to inspire us.\n\nBefore your journey, I only wanted to be an artist. Now I want to be an artist and a scientist. I want to paint the planets and study them too!\n\nCould you tell me what Earth looked like from space? Were you afraid during the launch?\n\nThank you for showing girls like me that our dreams can reach the stars.\n\nWith great respect,\n\nLayla","words":213,"limit":142}],"time_limit_sec":142},{"id":"RW-L05-U4-LS3-ORG","type":"organizer","organizer":"Motivation & Change Map","instructions":"Organizer: Complete each box for Sami (story) and Layla (letter).","items":[{"q":"At first (start + evidence)","answer":"Sami: hated storms, hid under his blanket · Layla: only wanted to be an artist"},{"q":"The event or person that made a difference","answer":"Sami: the SOS signal from Mr. Hamdan's house · Layla: watching Rayyanah Barnawi go to space"},{"q":"Motivation (why they act)","answer":"Sami: 'more afraid for Mr. Hamdan' – worry for his neighbor · Layla: admiration and thanks – 'you are my hero'"},{"q":"By the end (change + evidence)","answer":"Sami: didn't hide – 'He just listened' · Layla: wants to be an artist and a scientist"}]}],"game":{"name":"Before & After Hero Cards","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["On this screen: answer the lesson questions as fast as you can.","In class: Change machine: the child drops a 'before' card into a machine, chooses the event that changes it and the motivation, and the correct 'after' card comes out. Wrong choices jam the machine.","Teams get mixed before, after, event and motivation cards.","They build a full change chain for each character: before → event → motivation → after.","They explain one chain aloud with evidence.","Other teams check.","Each correct chain = 4 points; explanation with a quotation = 2 bonus points."],"data":[]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"In a story about heroes, what is a character's *motivation*?","answer":"the reason why the character does something","explanation":"Motivation.","explanation_ar":"الدافع.","options":["the place where the story happens","the reason why the character does something","the last event","the title"],"dok":1,"skill":"motivation"},{"q":"What is an *astronaut*?","answer":"a person who travels into space","explanation":"Glossary.","explanation_ar":"رائد فضاء.","options":["a person who studies rocks","a pilot of a plane","a person who travels into space","a sailor"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary"},{"q":"*Traveling to space is **risky**.* *Risky* means ___.","answer":"possibly dangerous","explanation":"Risky.","explanation_ar":"محفوف بالمخاطر.","options":["very cheap","very boring","very easy","possibly dangerous"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary in context"},{"q":"How does Layla close her letter?","answer":"With great respect, Layla","explanation":"Closing.","explanation_ar":"With great respect.","options":["Love, Mom","With great respect, Layla","The end.","Best wishes, Rayyanah"],"dok":1,"skill":"letter format"},{"q":"Which sentence about Layla's dream is correct?","answer":"Layla wants to be an artist and a scientist.","explanation":"wants to be.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["Layla wants to be an artist and a scientist.","Layla want to be an artist and a scientist.","Layla wanting to be an artist and a scientist.","Layla wants be an artist and a scientist."],"dok":2,"skill":"grammar"},{"q":"Which sentence about Sami's fear and his actions is correct?","answer":"Sami was afraid, but he helped.","explanation":"Past + comma + but.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["Sami was afraid but he help.","Sami is afraid, but he helped yesterday.","Sami was afraid, but he helped.","Sami were afraid, but he helped."],"dok":2,"skill":"grammar"},{"q":"What is the main PURPOSE of Layla's letter?","answer":"to express admiration and thanks to her hero","explanation":"Author's purpose.","explanation_ar":"التعبير عن الإعجاب والشكر.","options":["to give instructions for building a rocket","to express admiration and thanks to her hero","to persuade the school to buy a screen","to tell a funny story"],"dok":2,"skill":"author's purpose"},{"q":"Which detail shows that Layla's whole class admired the astronaut?","answer":"They cheered so loudly that the principal came to see what was happening.","explanation":"Evidence.","explanation_ar":"هتفوا بصوت عالٍ.","options":["They cheered so loudly that the principal came to see what was happening.","Layla lives in Taif.","The launch was in May 2023.","Layla wants to paint the planets."],"dok":2,"skill":"evidence"},{"q":"Which word BEST describes both Sami and Rayyanah Barnawi?","answer":"courageous","explanation":"Shared trait.","explanation_ar":"شجاع.","options":["lazy","selfish","careless","courageous"],"dok":3,"skill":"character traits"},{"q":"Why do heroes often cause OTHER people to change?","answer":"Their actions show others what is possible and inspire them to try.","explanation":"Theme across texts.","explanation_ar":"أفعالهم تلهم الآخرين.","options":["They give orders to everyone.","They are famous.","Their actions show others what is possible and inspire them to try.","They are always adults."],"dok":3,"skill":"theme"}],"images":[{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS3-V01","prompt":"Picture for the word 'astronaut': an astronaut in a space suit"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS3-V02","prompt":"Picture for the word 'launch': a rocket lifting off"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS3-V03","prompt":"Picture for the word 'research': a scientist with a microscope"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS3-V04","prompt":"Picture for the word 'risky': a warning sign"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS3-V05","prompt":"Picture for the word 'motivation': an arrow from a heart to an action"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS3-V06","prompt":"Picture for the word 'respect': a student bowing her head politely"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS3-V07","prompt":"Picture for the word 'dream': a child looking at the stars"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS3-01","prompt":"Students cheering at a rocket launch on a big screen."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS3-02","prompt":"Layla painting planets in her sketchbook."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS3-03","prompt":"A motivation and change map."}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS3-V01","script":"astronaut. She became the first Saudi woman astronaut."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS3-V02","script":"launch. We watched the launch on a big screen."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS3-V03","script":"research. She did research on cells."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS3-V04","script":"risky. Traveling to space is risky."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS3-V05","script":"motivation. Sami's motivation was to help his neighbor."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS3-V06","script":"respect. She signed the letter 'With great respect'."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS3-V07","script":"dream. Our dreams can reach the stars."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS3-T1","script":"Dear Ms. Rayyanah Barnawi, My name is Layla, and I am a student in Taif. I am writing to tell you that you are my hero. In May 2023, you became the first Saudi woman to travel to space. My whole class watched the launch on the big screen in the school hall. When the rocket lifted off, we cheered so loudly that the principal came to see what was happening! I admire you for three reasons. First, you were determined. Before you became an astronaut, you spent many years studying and doing research on cells in laboratories, and you did not give up when the work was hard. Second, you showed great courage. Traveling to the International Space Station is risky, but you went to help science. Third, you remembered children like me. From space, you did simple science experiments with students across Saudi Arabia to inspire us. Before your journey, I only wanted to be an artist. Now I want to be an artist and a scientist. I want to paint the planets and study them too! Could you tell me what Earth looked like from space? Were you afraid during the launch? Thank you for showing girls like me that our dreams can reach the stars. With great respect, Layla"},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS3-VID","script":"10… 9… 8… A rocket is about to launch – and a girl in Taif is about to change her dream! Dear Ms. Rayyanah Barnawi, My name is Layla… Motivation = WHY a character acts. Sami helped because he was worried about his neighbor. Change: At first … After … By the end … Sami became braver; Layla's dream grew bigger! Heroes inspire us to change. Who inspires YOU?"}]},{"id":"RW-L05-U4-LS4","title":"Writing Skill: Describing a person with examples","lesson_type":"writing_skill","objectives":["describe a person with exact trait words (generous, patient, humble, determined)","support each trait with a specific example: an action, a memory or the person's own words","link traits with transitions (First, For example, Another quality, Above all)"],"objectives_ar":["وصف شخص بصفات دقيقة.","دعم كل صفة بمثال محدد: فعل أو ذكرى أو كلام الشخص نفسه.","ربط الصفات بكلمات الانتقال."],"success_criteria":["I can choose exact trait words instead of nice or good.","I can give a specific example for each trait (who, what, when).","I can organize traits with transitions and end with what I learned."],"success_criteria_ar":["أستطيع اختيار صفات دقيقة بدل nice أو good.","أستطيع إعطاء مثال محدد لكل صفة.","أستطيع تنظيم الصفات بكلمات الانتقال وإنهاء الوصف بما تعلمته."],"map_area":"Language Usage: Write, Revise Texts for Purpose and Audience (cross-strand)","vocabulary":[{"word":"trait","pos":"noun","ipa":"/treɪt/","definition":"a quality that is part of a person's character","arabic":"صفة / سمة","example":"Patience is one of her best traits.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS4-V01","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS4-V01","tier":"core"},{"word":"generous","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈdʒɛnərəs/","definition":"happy to give time, money or help to others","arabic":"كريم","example":"My grandmother is generous with her food.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS4-V02","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS4-V02","tier":"core"},{"word":"patience","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈpeɪʃəns/","definition":"the ability to wait or keep trying calmly","arabic":"الصبر","example":"She taught me to read with great patience.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS4-V03","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS4-V03","tier":"core"},{"word":"quality","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈkwɑləti/","definition":"a good part of someone's character","arabic":"خصلة / صفة","example":"Honesty is an important quality.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS4-V04","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS4-V04","tier":"core"},{"word":"incredibly","pos":"adverb","ipa":"/ɪnˈkrɛdəbli/","definition":"very, very (much more than usual)","arabic":"بشكل لا يُصدّق / جدًا","example":"She is incredibly kind.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS4-V05","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS4-V05","tier":"core"},{"word":"specific","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/spəˈsɪfɪk/","definition":"exact and clear, not general","arabic":"محدد","example":"Give a specific example.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS4-V06","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS4-V06","tier":"core"},{"word":"helping hand","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈhɛlpɪŋ hænd/","definition":"help that you give someone","arabic":"يد العون","example":"She always gives a helping hand.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS4-V07","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS4-V07","tier":"core"}],"explanation":{"text":"When you describe a person, don't just say they are **nice** or **good**. Choose **exact trait words**: *generous, patient, humble, determined, honest, brave, responsible, cheerful, hard-working*.\n\nEvery trait needs a **specific example** – proof from real life. Good examples tell **what the person did**, **when** or **how often**, and sometimes **what they said**: *For example, every Thursday she cooks … and sends plates to three neighbors.*\n\nOrganize your description with **transitions**: *First, … For example, … Another quality I admire is … For instance, … Above all, …*. End with a **conclusion**: what you **learned** from this person or why they matter to you.","examples":["Vague: *My grandmother is nice.* → Exact: ***My grandmother is generous.***","Trait + example: ***She is generous. For example, every Thursday she cooks for three neighbors who live alone.***","Trait + memory: ***Another quality I admire is her patience. When I was seven, she taught me to read every evening for months.***","Trait + the person's words: ***Above all, she is humble. When people thank her, she just smiles and says, \"It is nothing.\"***","Determined: ***My brother is determined. He practiced the same piano piece for an hour every day until he could play it perfectly.***","Honest: ***My friend is honest. Last week, the cashier gave him too much change, and he gave it back.***","Show, don't tell: *She is hard-working.* → ***She wakes up at five every morning to prepare for her nursing exams.***","Strong adverb: ***She is incredibly patient.***","Conclusion: ***She taught me that you don't need to be famous to be a hero.***"],"common_errors":["✗ He is nice and good. → ✓ He is generous and honest. (Use exact traits.)","✗ A trait with no example. → ✓ Add: For example, … (Prove it!)","✗ A general example: She helps people. → ✓ A specific one: She drives our neighbor to the hospital every Monday. (Who? What? When?)","✗ She is very patience. → ✓ She is very patient. / She has great patience. (Adjective **patient**; noun **patience**.)","✗ For example she cooks… → ✓ For example, she cooks… (Comma after **For example**.)","✗ Another quality I admire is she is humble. → ✓ Another quality I admire is her humility. / She is also humble. (Use a noun after **is**.)","✗ My hero is my father he works hard. → ✓ My hero is my father. He works hard. (Two sentences.)"],"arabic":"عند وصف شخص لا تكتفِ بـ nice أو good، بل اختر صفات دقيقة مثل generous وpatient وhumble وdetermined.\n\nكل صفة تحتاج إلى مثال محدد من الواقع: ماذا فعل الشخص؟ متى أو كم مرة؟ وماذا قال أحيانًا؟\n\nنظّم الوصف بكلمات الانتقال: First, For example, Another quality I admire is, Above all، واختم بما تعلمته من هذا الشخص.\n\nانتبه: patient صفة، وpatience اسم، وضع فاصلة بعد For example."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:25","narration":"Some heroes are on the news. Others are in our own homes. Meet Noura's quiet hero!","on_screen":"Describing a Person 👵❤️","visual":"Noura and her grandmother cooking together."},{"time":"00:25–01:25","narration":"Some heroes rescue people from storms. My hero, my grandmother Hessa…","on_screen":"(Noura's model)","visual":"Grandmother Hessa sending plates to neighbors; teaching young Noura to read; smiling humbly."},{"time":"01:25–02:15","narration":"Nice? Good? Too vague! Try generous, patient, humble, determined!","on_screen":"Exact trait words","visual":"Vague words fade; exact words light up."},{"time":"02:15–03:05","narration":"Prove each trait with a specific example: what, when, how often – even their own words!","on_screen":"Trait + example 🔍","visual":"A trait card connects to a memory bubble."},{"time":"03:05–03:30","narration":"End with what your hero taught you.","on_screen":"What I learned 💡","visual":"Noura writes: 'a kind heart and a helping hand'."}],"captions_ar":["بعض الأبطال يظهرون في الأخبار، وآخرون في بيوتنا. تعرّف إلى بطلة نورة الهادئة!","بعض الأبطال ينقذون الناس من العواصف. بطلتي جدتي حصة…","لطيفة؟ جيدة؟ كلمات عامة! جرّب: كريمة، صبورة، متواضعة، مصممة!","أثبت كل صفة بمثال محدد: ماذا ومتى وكم مرة، بل وبكلماتهم!","اختم بما علّمك إياه بطلك."],"voice":"Narrator: American English, gentle female voice, speed 0.95. Noura reads her description."},"texts":[{"type":"model","title":"My Grandmother, the Quiet Hero (by Noura)","body":"Some heroes rescue people from storms. My hero, my grandmother Hessa, has never been on the news, but she has changed many lives.\n\nFirst, she is incredibly generous. For example, every Thursday she cooks a large pot of rice and chicken and sends plates to three neighbors who live alone. Another quality I admire is her patience. When I was seven, I could not read Arabic well, so she sat with me every evening for months until I could read a whole story by myself. Above all, she is humble. When people thank her, she just smiles and says, \"It is nothing.\" My grandmother has taught me that you don't need to be famous to be a hero – you just need a kind heart and a helping hand.","word_count":128,"audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS4-T1","id":"TXT-RW-L05-U4-LS4-1","genre":"model text","role":"model","difficulty":"550L–750L","glossary":[],"annotations":["**Introduction:** a contrast hook (*Some heroes rescue people from storms*) + who the hero is.","**Trait 1 + example:** *generous* → *every Thursday she cooks … and sends plates to three neighbors* (a specific action with a time and numbers).","**Trait 2 + example:** *patience* → *she sat with me every evening for months* (a personal memory).","**Trait 3 + example:** *humble* → *she just smiles and says, \"It is nothing.\"* (her own words).","**Transitions:** *First, For example, Another quality I admire is, Above all*.","**Exact trait words:** *generous, patient, humble* – not just *nice* or *good*.","**Conclusion:** what the writer learned from the hero."]}],"activities":[{"id":"RW-L05-U4-LS4-A1","type":"mcq","stage":"controlled","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read Noura's description. Choose the best answer.","instructions_ar":"اقرأ وصف نورة واختر أفضل إجابة.","items":[{"q":"Who is Noura's hero?","answer":"her grandmother Hessa","explanation":"Introduction.","explanation_ar":"جدتها حصة.","options":["a famous astronaut","her teacher","her grandmother Hessa","a firefighter"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"What does Grandmother Hessa do every Thursday?","answer":"She cooks and sends plates to three neighbors who live alone.","explanation":"Example 1.","explanation_ar":"تطبخ وترسل أطباقًا لجيرانها.","options":["She cooks and sends plates to three neighbors who live alone.","She goes shopping in the souq.","She visits the hospital.","She teaches at a school."],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"How did she show patience?","answer":"She helped Noura learn to read every evening for months.","explanation":"Example 2.","explanation_ar":"علّمت نورة القراءة شهورًا.","options":["She waited for a bus.","She helped Noura learn to read every evening for months.","She cooked slowly.","She listened to the radio."],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"What does she say when people thank her?","answer":"\"It is nothing.\"","explanation":"Example 3.","explanation_ar":"«لا شيء».","options":["\"Thank you very much.\"","\"I am the best.\"","\"Give me a prize.\"","\"It is nothing.\""],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Which trait does *It is nothing* show?","answer":"humility (she is humble)","explanation":"Trait + words.","explanation_ar":"التواضع.","options":["humility (she is humble)","anger","fear","laziness"],"dok":2,"skill":"character traits","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"What did Noura learn from her grandmother?","answer":"You don't need to be famous to be a hero.","explanation":"Conclusion.","explanation_ar":"لا يلزم أن تكون مشهورًا لتكون بطلًا.","options":["Cooking is easy.","Reading is boring.","You don't need to be famous to be a hero.","Heroes must be on the news."],"dok":2,"skill":"conclusions","stage":"controlled"}]},{"id":"RW-L05-U4-LS4-A2","type":"mcq","stage":"guided","instructions":"Guided practice: Traits and examples. Choose.","instructions_ar":"الصفات والأمثلة: اختر.","items":[{"q":"Which sentence uses an EXACT trait word instead of a vague one?","answer":"My uncle is generous.","explanation":"Exact trait.","explanation_ar":"صفة دقيقة.","options":["My uncle is generous.","My uncle is nice.","My uncle is good.","My uncle is okay."],"dok":1,"skill":"word choice","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which example BEST proves that a brother is *determined*?","answer":"He practiced the same piece on the piano for an hour every day until he could play it perfectly.","explanation":"Specific example.","explanation_ar":"المثال الأقوى.","options":["He likes music.","He is tall.","He has a piano.","He practiced the same piece on the piano for an hour every day until he could play it perfectly."],"dok":2,"skill":"examples","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which example is the MOST specific for a *helpful* neighbor?","answer":"Every Monday, she drives our elderly neighbor to the hospital.","explanation":"Who, what, when.","explanation_ar":"الأكثر تحديدًا.","options":["She helps people.","Every Monday, she drives our elderly neighbor to the hospital.","She is helpful.","She is a good neighbor."],"dok":2,"skill":"examples","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which sentence about Grandmother Hessa's patience is written correctly?","answer":"She is very patient.","explanation":"Adjective form.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["She is very patience.","She is very patient.","She is very patiently.","She very patient is."],"dok":2,"skill":"grammar","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which transition introduces the MOST important trait?","answer":"Above all,","explanation":"Transition.","explanation_ar":"Above all.","options":["First,","For example,","Another quality I admire is","Above all,"],"dok":2,"skill":"transitions","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which sentence SHOWS that a mother is hard-working instead of telling it?","answer":"She wakes up at five every morning to study for her nursing exams.","explanation":"Show, don't tell.","explanation_ar":"يُظهر الاجتهاد.","options":["She is very hard-working.","She works hard.","She wakes up at five every morning to study for her nursing exams.","She is a hard-working mother."],"dok":3,"skill":"show, don't tell","stage":"guided"}]},{"id":"RW-L05-U4-LS4-A3","type":"gap_fill","stage":"freer","instructions":"Freer practice: Complete the description with the word bank.","instructions_ar":"أكمل الوصف من بنك الكلمات.","items":[{"q":"My father is incredibly ________. He gives his time to help anyone who asks.","answer":"generous","explanation":"Trait.","explanation_ar":"كريم.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"________, every Friday he volunteers at the mosque's charity kitchen.","answer":"For example","explanation":"Example.","explanation_ar":"على سبيل المثال.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"________ I admire is his honesty.","answer":"Another quality","explanation":"Transition.","explanation_ar":"خصلة أخرى.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"He always tells the truth, even when it is difficult. He has great ________.","answer":"integrity","explanation":"Honesty.","explanation_ar":"نزاهة.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"________, he is humble and never talks about his good deeds.","answer":"Above all","explanation":"Most important.","explanation_ar":"وفوق كل شيء.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Please give a ________ example, not a general one.","answer":"specific","explanation":"Exact.","explanation_ar":"محدد.","stage":"freer"}]},{"id":"RW-L05-U4-LS4-A4","type":"open","stage":"production","instructions":"Writing: Describe a person.","instructions_ar":"صِف شخصًا.","items":[{"q":"Turn this vague sentence into a trait + specific example: *My teacher is nice.*","answer":"My teacher is patient. For example, she explains a math problem three times without getting angry.","explanation":"Trait + example.","explanation_ar":"صفة + مثال.","dok":2,"skill":"examples","stage":"production"},{"q":"Write a trait and an example that uses the person's own words.","answer":"My coach is encouraging. When I miss a goal, he always says, \"Next time, it's yours!\"","explanation":"Trait + words.","explanation_ar":"صفة + كلامه.","dok":2,"skill":"examples","stage":"production"},{"q":"Write a 'show, don't tell' sentence for *brave*.","answer":"My cousin held my hand and walked me past the barking dog, even though she was shaking.","explanation":"Show.","explanation_ar":"أظهِر.","dok":3,"skill":"show, don't tell","stage":"production"},{"q":"Write a conclusion sentence: what did your hero teach you?","answer":"My father taught me that real heroes help others quietly, without asking for thanks.","explanation":"Conclusion.","explanation_ar":"خاتمة.","dok":2,"skill":"conclusions","stage":"production"}]}],"game":{"name":"Hero Trading Cards","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["On this screen: answer the lesson questions as fast as you can.","In class: Card maker: the child chooses a hero picture, picks three exact traits and types a specific example for each. The app flags vague words (nice, good) and asks 'When? How often?' to make the examples stronger.","Each student makes a hero card: name, three traits and one specific example for each.","Students trade cards in a group.","Readers check: Are the traits exact? Are the examples specific?","Each reader gives one 'star' (strong example) and one 'wish' (make it more specific).","Cards with three strong examples go on the class 'Hall of Heroes'."],"data":[]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"What is a *trait*?","answer":"a quality that is part of a person's character","explanation":"Trait.","explanation_ar":"صفة.","options":["a kind of train","a place","a memory","a quality that is part of a person's character"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary"},{"q":"Which trait word is MORE exact than *nice*?","answer":"generous","explanation":"Exact word.","explanation_ar":"generous.","options":["good","generous","okay","fine"],"dok":1,"skill":"word choice"},{"q":"*Give a **specific** example.* *Specific* means ___.","answer":"exact and clear","explanation":"Specific.","explanation_ar":"محدد.","options":["long and boring","exact and clear","general","funny"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary in context"},{"q":"Which transition introduces an EXAMPLE?","answer":"For example,","explanation":"Transition.","explanation_ar":"For example.","options":["Above all,","In conclusion,","However,","For example,"],"dok":1,"skill":"transitions"},{"q":"Which sentence about Grandmother Hessa's cooking is written correctly?","answer":"For example, she cooks for her neighbors every Thursday.","explanation":"Comma.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["For example, she cooks for her neighbors every Thursday.","For example she cooks for her neighbors every Thursday.","For, example she cooks for her neighbors.","For example she, cooks for her neighbors."],"dok":2,"skill":"punctuation"},{"q":"Which sentence uses *patience* correctly?","answer":"She taught me with great patience.","explanation":"Noun form.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["She is very patience.","She patience waited.","She taught me with great patience.","She was patience with me."],"dok":2,"skill":"grammar"},{"q":"Which example BEST proves that someone is *honest*?","answer":"When the cashier gave him too much change, he gave it back.","explanation":"Specific example.","explanation_ar":"المثال الأفضل.","options":["He has a big house.","He likes football.","He is my friend.","When the cashier gave him too much change, he gave it back."],"dok":2,"skill":"examples"},{"q":"Why does Noura begin with *Some heroes rescue people from storms*?","answer":"to contrast famous heroes with her quiet, everyday hero","explanation":"Hook.","explanation_ar":"لتقارن الأبطال المشهورين ببطلتها.","options":["to tell a story about a storm","to list her grandmother's food","to contrast famous heroes with her quiet, everyday hero","to give a fact about weather"],"dok":3,"skill":"author's craft"},{"q":"A description says only: *She helps people.* What is the BEST improvement?","answer":"Add who she helps, how and how often.","explanation":"Revising.","explanation_ar":"أضف تفاصيل محددة.","options":["Add who she helps, how and how often.","Add more exclamation marks.","Make it shorter.","Change *she* to *he*."],"dok":2,"skill":"revising"},{"q":"Which is the strongest CONCLUSION for a description of a hero?","answer":"He taught me that real courage means helping others quietly.","explanation":"Conclusion.","explanation_ar":"أقوى خاتمة.","options":["He has brown hair.","He taught me that real courage means helping others quietly.","He was born in Riyadh.","He likes coffee."],"dok":3,"skill":"conclusions"}],"images":[{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS4-V01","prompt":"Picture for the word 'trait': a person with icons of a heart and a clock"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS4-V02","prompt":"Picture for the word 'generous': a woman handing out plates of food"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS4-V03","prompt":"Picture for the word 'patience': a grandmother helping a child read"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS4-V04","prompt":"Picture for the word 'quality': a star badge on a person"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS4-V05","prompt":"Picture for the word 'incredibly': a big heart icon"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS4-V06","prompt":"Picture for the word 'specific': a magnifying glass on one detail"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS4-V07","prompt":"Picture for the word 'helping hand': two hands reaching to help"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS4-01","prompt":"A grandmother cooking for neighbors and teaching her granddaughter to read."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS4-02","prompt":"A trait connected to a specific example."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS4-03","prompt":"A wall of hero trading cards."}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS4-V01","script":"trait. Patience is one of her best traits."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS4-V02","script":"generous. My grandmother is generous with her food."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS4-V03","script":"patience. She taught me to read with great patience."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS4-V04","script":"quality. Honesty is an important quality."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS4-V05","script":"incredibly. She is incredibly kind."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS4-V06","script":"specific. Give a specific example."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS4-V07","script":"helping hand. She always gives a helping hand."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS4-T1","script":"Some heroes rescue people from storms. My hero, my grandmother Hessa, has never been on the news, but she has changed many lives. First, she is incredibly generous. For example, every Thursday she cooks a large pot of rice and chicken and sends plates to three neighbors who live alone. Another quality I admire is her patience. When I was seven, I could not read Arabic well, so she sat with me every evening for months until I could read a whole story by myself. Above all, she is humble. When people thank her, she just smiles and says, \"It is nothing.\" My grandmother has taught me that you don't need to be famous to be a hero – you just need a kind heart and a helping hand."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS4-VID","script":"Some heroes are on the news. Others are in our own homes. Meet Noura's quiet hero! Some heroes rescue people from storms. My hero, my grandmother Hessa… Nice? Good? Too vague! Try generous, patient, humble, determined! Prove each trait with a specific example: what, when, how often – even their own words! End with what your hero taught you."}]},{"id":"RW-L05-U4-LS5","title":"Writing Workshop: My Hero","lesson_type":"writing_workshop","objectives":["plan a two-paragraph descriptive text about a hero with the Hero Profile Planner","write 120–150 words with a hook, three exact traits, specific examples and a conclusion","revise, edit and publish 'My Hero' on the class Hall of Heroes"],"objectives_ar":["التخطيط لنص وصفي من فقرتين عن بطل بمخطط ملف البطل.","كتابة 120–150 كلمة فيها جملة جذب وثلاث صفات دقيقة وأمثلة محددة وخاتمة.","تحسين النص وتدقيقه ونشره في «قاعة الأبطال» في الصف."],"success_criteria":["Paragraph 1 has a hook and tells who my hero is and why he or she matters to me.","Paragraph 2 has three exact traits, each with a specific example, and transitions.","My conclusion tells what I learned, and my text is 120–150 words."],"success_criteria_ar":["الفقرة الأولى فيها جملة جذب وتذكر من بطلي ولماذا هو مهم لي.","الفقرة الثانية فيها ثلاث صفات دقيقة لكل منها مثال محدد مع كلمات انتقال.","خاتمتي تذكر ما تعلمته، ونصي 120–150 كلمة."],"map_area":"Language Usage: Write, Revise Texts for Purpose and Audience (cross-strand)","vocabulary":[{"word":"civil defense","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈsɪvəl dɪˈfɛns/","definition":"the government service that protects people in emergencies like fires and floods","arabic":"الدفاع المدني","example":"My uncle works for the civil defense.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS5-V01","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS5-V01","tier":"core"},{"word":"retired","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/rɪˈtaɪərd/","definition":"no longer working because of age","arabic":"متقاعد","example":"Mrs. Amal is a retired teacher.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS5-V02","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS5-V02","tier":"core"},{"word":"leftover","pos":"adjective / noun","ipa":"/ˈlɛftˌoʊvər/","definition":"remaining after the rest has been used","arabic":"متبقٍّ / بقايا","example":"He gives the leftover bread to workers.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS5-V03","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS5-V03","tier":"core"},{"word":"encouraging","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ɪnˈkɝɪdʒɪŋ/","definition":"giving someone hope and confidence","arabic":"مشجّع","example":"Our coach is always encouraging.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS5-V04","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS5-V04","tier":"core"},{"word":"fair","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/fɛr/","definition":"treating everyone equally and in the right way","arabic":"عادل / منصف","example":"A fair coach gives everyone a chance.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS5-V05","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS5-V05","tier":"core"},{"word":"apron","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈeɪprən/","definition":"a piece of cloth you wear over your clothes to keep them clean while cooking","arabic":"مريلة","example":"The baker wore a white apron.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS5-V06","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS5-V06","tier":"core"},{"word":"profile","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈproʊfaɪl/","definition":"a short description of a person","arabic":"نبذة / ملف تعريفي","example":"Write a profile of your hero.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS5-V07","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS5-V07","tier":"core"}],"explanation":{"text":"Your text describes **one real hero** so that readers understand **who** this person is and **why** he or she is a hero. Choose someone you know well – a family member, a teacher, a neighbor or a community helper.\n\n**Paragraph 1:** a **hook** (a vivid detail, a question or a contrast) + **who** your hero is and **how you know** him or her. **Paragraph 2:** **three exact traits**, each with a **specific example** (an action, a memory or the person's own words), linked with **transitions** (*First, For example, Another quality, Above all*), and a **conclusion**: what you **learned**.\n\nUse **exact words** (generous, determined, encouraging) and **show, don't tell**. Keep it **120–150 words**, and check that each example answers **What? When? How often?**","examples":["Hook (vivid detail): ***Every morning at five o'clock, when our street is still dark, one window is already glowing.***","Who + relationship: ***That is Mr. Yousef's bakery, and Mr. Yousef is my hero.***","Trait 1 + example: ***Mr. Yousef is hard-working. For example, he has baked bread six days a week for more than twenty years.***","Trait 2 + example: ***He is also generous. Every evening, he gives the leftover bread to the workers who clean our streets.***","Trait 3 + own words: ***Above all, he is kind to children. When I forgot my money last month, he handed me a warm bag of bread and said, \"Pay me tomorrow, my son.\"***","Conclusion with a metaphor: ***Mr. Yousef has taught me that heroes do not need capes – sometimes they just need an apron and a big heart.***","Another hook (question): ***What makes a hero? For me, the answer is my uncle Fahd.***","Another hook (contrast): ***Some heroes fly in movies; mine teaches reading on Saturday mornings.***","Paragraph break: start Paragraph 2 with the first trait."],"common_errors":["✗ Writing about a superhero from a cartoon. → ✓ Choose a real person you know. (Real heroes!)","✗ Listing traits with no examples. → ✓ Add a specific example for each trait. (Prove each trait.)","✗ Telling the person's whole life story. → ✓ Focus on three traits and examples. (Stay focused.)","✗ He is hard-work. → ✓ He is hard-working. (Adjective: **hard-working**.)","✗ He gave to me a bag of bread. → ✓ He gave me a bag of bread. (give + person + thing.)","✗ No conclusion. → ✓ End with what you learned from your hero. (Close the circle.)","✗ He has baked bread since twenty years. → ✓ He has baked bread for twenty years. (**for** + a period of time.)"],"arabic":"يصف نصك بطلًا حقيقيًا واحدًا ليفهم القارئ من هو ولماذا هو بطل؛ اختر شخصًا تعرفه جيدًا.\n\nالفقرة الأولى: جملة جذب + من هو بطلك وكيف تعرفه. الفقرة الثانية: ثلاث صفات دقيقة لكل منها مثال محدد مع كلمات الانتقال، ثم خاتمة بما تعلمته.\n\nاستخدم كلمات دقيقة وأظهِر ولا تُخبر، والتزم بطول 120–150 كلمة.\n\nانتبه: for twenty years (مدة)، وgave me a bag (أعطاني كيسًا)."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:25","narration":"Who is the hero in YOUR life? Today, you will tell the world!","on_screen":"My Hero 🦸‍♂️","visual":"Omar walks down his street at dawn toward a glowing bakery window."},{"time":"00:25–01:05","narration":"Read the interview notes: a civil-defense officer, a retired teacher, a baker, a coach – or interview your own hero!","on_screen":"Hero Interview Notes","visual":"Four cards with portraits appear."},{"time":"01:05–02:05","narration":"Every morning at five o'clock, when our street is still dark, one window is already glowing…","on_screen":"(model)","visual":"Mr. Yousef baking; giving bread to street cleaners; handing Omar a warm bag."},{"time":"02:05–02:55","narration":"Paragraph 1: hook + who. Paragraph 2: three traits with examples + what you learned!","on_screen":"P1: Hook + Who · P2: Traits + Examples + Lesson","visual":"Two blocks build with labels."},{"time":"02:55–03:30","narration":"Publish your hero on our Hall of Heroes!","on_screen":"Hall of Heroes 🏅","visual":"Student posters appear on a classroom wall."}],"captions_ar":["من البطل في حياتك؟ اليوم ستخبر العالم!","اقرأ ملاحظات المقابلات: ضابط دفاع مدني، ومعلمة متقاعدة، وخبّاز، ومدرب، أو قابل بطلك أنت!","كل صباح في الخامسة، حين يكون شارعنا مظلمًا، تكون نافذة واحدة مضاءة…","الفقرة الأولى: جذب + من هو. الفقرة الثانية: ثلاث صفات بأمثلة + ما تعلمته!","انشر بطلك في قاعة الأبطال!"],"voice":"Narrator: American English, warm male voice, speed 0.95. Omar reads the model."},"texts":[{"type":"model","title":"Hero Interview Notes","body":"**Card A – Uncle Fahd, civil-defense officer** · Traits: brave, calm, responsible · Examples: helped rescue families during heavy rain last winter; teaches fire-safety lessons at schools · His words: \"Stay calm – panic never helped anyone.\"\n\n**Card B – Mrs. Amal, retired teacher** · Traits: patient, generous, wise · Examples: teaches reading to neighborhood children for free every Saturday; lends books from her own shelves · Her words: \"A book is a friend that never leaves you.\"\n\n**Card C – Mr. Yousef, the baker** · Traits: hard-working, generous, kind · Examples: has baked bread six days a week for more than twenty years; gives leftover bread to street cleaners every evening · His words: \"Pay me tomorrow, my son.\"\n\n**Card D – Coach Saad** · Traits: encouraging, fair, determined · Examples: trains the school team after school even in the summer heat; gives every player a chance · His words: \"Mistakes are the first step to getting better.\"","word_count":142,"audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS5-T1","id":"TXT-RW-L05-U4-LS5-1","genre":"interview notes","role":"model","difficulty":"550L–750L","glossary":[],"annotations":["Choose **one card**, or interview a real hero in your own life and make notes like these.","Choose **three exact traits** and a **specific example** for each – one example can be the person's **own words**.","Plan **two paragraphs**: (1) a hook + who your hero is; (2) traits with examples + what you learned."]}],"activities":[{"id":"RW-L05-U4-LS5-A1","type":"mcq","stage":"controlled","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read the interview notes and the model. Choose the answer.","instructions_ar":"اقرأ الملاحظات والنموذج واختر الإجابة.","items":[{"q":"What does Mrs. Amal do every Saturday (Card B)?","answer":"She teaches reading to neighborhood children for free.","explanation":"Card B.","explanation_ar":"تعلّم الأطفال القراءة مجانًا.","options":["She bakes bread.","She trains the football team.","She teaches reading to neighborhood children for free.","She teaches fire safety."],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Which hero says, *Stay calm – panic never helped anyone*?","answer":"Uncle Fahd","explanation":"Card A.","explanation_ar":"العم فهد.","options":["Mrs. Amal","Uncle Fahd","Mr. Yousef","Coach Saad"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"How long has Mr. Yousef baked bread?","answer":"for more than twenty years","explanation":"Card C / model.","explanation_ar":"أكثر من عشرين سنة.","options":["for more than twenty years","for two years","for one month","since last week"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Who receives Mr. Yousef's leftover bread?","answer":"the workers who clean the streets","explanation":"Model.","explanation_ar":"عمال النظافة.","options":["his family only","the school team","the civil defense","the workers who clean the streets"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Which hook does the model use?","answer":"a vivid detail about a glowing window at 5 a.m.","explanation":"Hook.","explanation_ar":"تفصيل حي.","options":["a question about capes","a joke","a vivid detail about a glowing window at 5 a.m.","a list of traits"],"dok":2,"skill":"hooks","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"What does *heroes do not need capes – sometimes they just need an apron and a big heart* mean?","answer":"Everyday people can be heroes through kindness and hard work.","explanation":"Metaphor.","explanation_ar":"الناس العاديون قد يكونون أبطالًا.","options":["Everyday people can be heroes through kindness and hard work.","Heroes must wear aprons.","Capes are expensive.","Bakers can fly."],"dok":3,"skill":"figurative language","stage":"controlled"}]},{"id":"RW-L05-U4-LS5-A2","type":"mcq","stage":"guided","instructions":"Guided practice: Plan your hero text. Choose.","instructions_ar":"خطّط لنص البطل: اختر.","items":[{"q":"Which is the BEST hook for a text about Coach Saad (Card D)?","answer":"In the summer heat, when everyone else has gone home, one man is still on the football field.","explanation":"Strong hook.","explanation_ar":"الأفضل.","options":["In the summer heat, when everyone else has gone home, one man is still on the football field.","My coach is nice.","This text is about my coach.","Coach Saad has a whistle."],"dok":1,"skill":"hooks","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which example BEST shows that Coach Saad is *fair*?","answer":"He gives every player a chance to play, not only the best ones.","explanation":"Specific example.","explanation_ar":"المثال الأفضل.","options":["He wears a cap.","He likes football.","He has a loud whistle.","He gives every player a chance to play, not only the best ones."],"dok":2,"skill":"examples","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which sentence about Mrs. Amal uses the hero's OWN WORDS as an example?","answer":"She often says, \"A book is a friend that never leaves you.\"","explanation":"Own words.","explanation_ar":"كلامها.","options":["She is a retired teacher.","She likes books.","She often says, \"A book is a friend that never leaves you.\"","She is old."],"dok":2,"skill":"examples","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which sentence about Mr. Yousef is correct?","answer":"He has baked bread for more than twenty years.","explanation":"for + period.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["He has baked bread since more than twenty years.","He has baked bread for more than twenty years.","He has bake bread for twenty years.","He baked bread for since twenty years."],"dok":2,"skill":"grammar","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Where should Paragraph 2 begin in the hero text?","answer":"with the first trait (First, …)","explanation":"Paragraphing.","explanation_ar":"عند الصفة الأولى.","options":["with the hook","with the conclusion","with the first trait (First, …)","in the middle of the hook sentence"],"dok":2,"skill":"paragraphing","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which conclusion about Uncle Fahd is the STRONGEST?","answer":"Uncle Fahd taught me that staying calm in danger can save lives.","explanation":"Lesson learned.","explanation_ar":"أقوى خاتمة.","options":["Uncle Fahd has a uniform.","That's all about Uncle Fahd.","Uncle Fahd likes tea.","Uncle Fahd taught me that staying calm in danger can save lives."],"dok":3,"skill":"conclusions","stage":"guided"}]},{"id":"RW-L05-U4-LS5-A3","type":"organizer","stage":"freer","instructions":"Organizer: Plan your text with the Hero Profile Planner.","instructions_ar":"خطط لنصك بمخطط ملف البطل.","items":[{"q":"Hook and who – write notes.","answer":"Hook: Some heroes fly in movies; mine teaches reading on Saturdays. Who: Mrs. Amal, our retired neighbor.","explanation":"Hook + who.","explanation_ar":"جذب + من.","dok":1,"skill":"planning","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Trait 1 + example – write notes.","answer":"patient – teaches children to read every Saturday, even the slow readers like me","explanation":"Trait 1.","explanation_ar":"الصفة 1.","dok":2,"skill":"planning","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Trait 2 + example and Trait 3 + own words – write notes.","answer":"generous – lends books from her own shelves; wise – 'A book is a friend that never leaves you.'","explanation":"Traits 2–3.","explanation_ar":"الصفتان 2–3.","dok":2,"skill":"planning","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Conclusion – what did you learn? (notes)","answer":"you can be a hero by sharing what you know","explanation":"Conclusion.","explanation_ar":"الخاتمة.","dok":2,"skill":"planning","stage":"freer"}]},{"id":"RW-L05-U4-LS5-A4","type":"writing","stage":"production","instructions":"Writing: Write, revise, edit and publish your hero text.","instructions_ar":"اكتب نص بطلك وحسّنه ودققه وانشره.","items":[{"q":"Write Paragraph 1: your hook and who your hero is.","answer":"Some heroes fly in movies; mine teaches reading on Saturday mornings. Her name is Mrs. Amal, and she is our retired neighbor.","explanation":"Paragraph 1.","explanation_ar":"الفقرة الأولى.","dok":2,"skill":"writing","stage":"production"},{"q":"Write Paragraph 2: three traits with specific examples.","answer":"First, she is patient. For example, she helped me read a whole book, one page at a time, for three months. She is also generous, because she lends us books from her own shelves. Above all, she is wise. She always says, \"A book is a friend that never leaves you.\"","explanation":"Paragraph 2.","explanation_ar":"الفقرة الثانية.","dok":2,"skill":"writing","stage":"production"},{"q":"Write your conclusion.","answer":"Mrs. Amal has taught me that sharing what you know is a quiet kind of heroism.","explanation":"Conclusion.","explanation_ar":"الخاتمة.","dok":3,"skill":"writing","stage":"production"},{"q":"Write one example you made more specific after the Two-Partner Edit (before → after).","answer":"Before: She helps children. After: Every Saturday, she teaches six neighborhood children to read for free.","explanation":"Revision.","explanation_ar":"تحسين.","dok":3,"skill":"revising","stage":"production","_w":{"checklist":[],"min":null,"max":null}}]},{"id":"RW-L05-U4-LS5-ORG","type":"organizer","organizer":"Hero Profile Planner","instructions":"Organizer: Use a card or your own interview notes. Write short notes in each box.","items":[{"q":"Hook (vivid detail, question or contrast)","answer":"5 a.m., street still dark, one window glowing"},{"q":"Who is my hero? How do I know him/her?","answer":"Mr. Yousef, the baker on our street"},{"q":"Trait 1 + specific example","answer":"hard-working – six days a week for more than twenty years"},{"q":"Trait 2 + specific example","answer":"generous – leftover bread to street cleaners every evening"},{"q":"Trait 3 + example or the hero's own words","answer":"kind to children – 'Pay me tomorrow, my son.'"},{"q":"Conclusion – what I learned","answer":"heroes don't need capes – an apron and a big heart"}]},{"id":"RW-L05-U4-LS5-WR","type":"writing","instructions":"Writing: Write a two-paragraph descriptive text called 'My Hero' (120–150 words) about a real person. Paragraph 1: a hook and who your hero is. Paragraph 2: three exact traits with specific examples (one can be the hero's own words), transitions and a conclusion about what you learned. Write a two-paragraph descriptive text called 'My Hero' (120–150 words) about a real person. Paragraph 1: a hook and who your hero is. Paragraph 2: three exact traits with specific examples (one can be the hero's own words), transitions and a conclusion about what you learned.","instructions_ar":"اكتب نصًا وصفيًا من فقرتين بعنوان «بطلي» (120–150 كلمة) عن شخص حقيقي. الفقرة الأولى: جملة جذب ومن هو بطلك. الفقرة الثانية: ثلاث صفات دقيقة بأمثلة محددة (أحدها قد يكون كلام البطل نفسه) مع كلمات الانتقال وخاتمة بما تعلمته.","prompt":"Write a two-paragraph descriptive text called 'My Hero' (120–150 words) about a real person. Paragraph 1: a hook and who your hero is. Paragraph 2: three exact traits with specific examples (one can be the hero's own words), transitions and a conclusion about what you learned.","checklist":["My hook makes the reader curious.","Paragraph 1 tells who my hero is and how I know him or her.","I used three exact trait words (not nice or good).","Each trait has a specific example (what, when, how often).","I used transitions (First, For example, Another quality, Above all).","I wrote a conclusion about what I learned.","My text has two paragraphs and 120–150 words.","I checked grammar (for + time, gave me), spelling and punctuation."],"rubric_id":"RW-RUBRIC-5T","min_words":120,"max_words":170,"organizer":"Hero Profile Planner (hook – who – trait 1 – trait 2 – trait 3 – conclusion)","items":[{"q":"Write a two-paragraph descriptive text called 'My Hero' (120–150 words) about a real person. Paragraph 1: a hook and who your hero is. Paragraph 2: three exact traits with specific examples (one can be the hero's own words), transitions and a conclusion about what you learned.","answer":"Every morning at five o'clock, when our street is still dark, one window is already glowing. That is Mr. Yousef's bakery, and Mr. Yousef is my hero. (new paragraph) First, Mr. Yousef is hard-working. For example, he has baked bread six days a week for more than twenty years, and he has never missed a morning. He is also generous. Every evening, he gives the leftover bread to the workers who clean our streets. Above all, he is kind to children. When I forgot my money last month, he handed me a warm bag of bread and said, \"Pay me tomorrow, my son.\" Mr. Yousef has taught me that heroes do not need capes – sometimes they just need an apron and a big heart.","_w":{"checklist":["My hook makes the reader curious.","Paragraph 1 tells who my hero is and how I know him or her.","I used three exact trait words (not nice or good).","Each trait has a specific example (what, when, how often).","I used transitions (First, For example, Another quality, Above all).","I wrote a conclusion about what I learned.","My text has two paragraphs and 120–150 words.","I checked grammar (for + time, gave me), spelling and punctuation."],"min":120,"max":170}}]}],"game":{"name":"Hall of Heroes Gallery","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["On this screen: answer the lesson questions as fast as you can.","In class: Gallery walk: the child reads three hero profiles, taps the exact traits and specific examples, and awards a medal to the most specific example. The app shows which examples answer What? When? How often?","Posters are displayed like a gallery.","Students walk in pairs and read three posters.","They add a sticky note: one exact trait, one strong example and one comment on the conclusion.","Each student gives one Hero Medal to the strongest example.","The poster with the most medals is read aloud to the class."],"data":[]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"What should Paragraph 1 of *My Hero* include?","answer":"a hook and who your hero is","explanation":"Organization.","explanation_ar":"جملة جذب ومن هو البطل.","options":["only the conclusion","a hook and who your hero is","a list of ten traits","the hero's address"],"dok":1,"skill":"organization"},{"q":"*Mrs. Amal is a **retired** teacher.* *Retired* means ___.","answer":"no longer working because of age","explanation":"Retired.","explanation_ar":"متقاعدة.","options":["no longer working because of age","very young","new at her job","angry"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary in context"},{"q":"What does a *civil-defense* officer do?","answer":"protects people in emergencies like fires and floods","explanation":"Vocabulary.","explanation_ar":"يحمي الناس في الطوارئ.","options":["bakes bread","teaches reading","trains football teams","protects people in emergencies like fires and floods"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary"},{"q":"How many traits should Paragraph 2 describe?","answer":"three","explanation":"Task.","explanation_ar":"ثلاث.","options":["one","ten","three","none"],"dok":1,"skill":"organization"},{"q":"Which sentence about the coach is correct?","answer":"The coach gave me a new chance.","explanation":"give + person + thing.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["The coach gave to me a new chance.","The coach given me a new chance.","The coach gave a new chance me.","The coach gave me a new chance."],"dok":2,"skill":"grammar"},{"q":"Which example is the MOST specific for *encouraging*?","answer":"When I missed a penalty, Coach Saad said, \"Mistakes are the first step to getting better.\"","explanation":"Specific example.","explanation_ar":"الأكثر تحديدًا.","options":["When I missed a penalty, Coach Saad said, \"Mistakes are the first step to getting better.\"","Coach Saad encourages people.","Coach Saad is nice.","Coach Saad is a coach."],"dok":2,"skill":"examples"},{"q":"Which transition introduces the LAST and most important trait?","answer":"Above all,","explanation":"Transition.","explanation_ar":"Above all.","options":["For example,","First,","Above all,","Every morning,"],"dok":2,"skill":"transitions"},{"q":"Why should you choose a REAL person for this text?","answer":"Real examples make the description true and meaningful.","explanation":"Purpose.","explanation_ar":"الأمثلة الحقيقية تجعله صادقًا وذا معنى.","options":["Cartoon heroes are not allowed in books.","Real examples make the description true and meaningful.","Real people are always famous.","It makes the text shorter."],"dok":2,"skill":"purpose"},{"q":"A partner says, *Your text tells his whole life from birth.* What should you do?","answer":"Focus on three traits with specific examples.","explanation":"Revising.","explanation_ar":"ركّز على ثلاث صفات.","options":["Add even more of his life story.","Focus on three traits with specific examples.","Remove all the examples.","Write it in one sentence."],"dok":3,"skill":"revising"},{"q":"Which conclusion uses a METAPHOR?","answer":"My uncle is a lighthouse for our whole family.","explanation":"Metaphor.","explanation_ar":"استعارة.","options":["My uncle is a lighthouse for our whole family.","My uncle is tall.","My uncle works hard.","My uncle likes tea."],"dok":3,"skill":"figurative language"}],"images":[{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS5-V01","prompt":"Picture for the word 'civil defense': a civil-defense officer in uniform"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS5-V02","prompt":"Picture for the word 'retired': an elderly woman reading at home"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS5-V03","prompt":"Picture for the word 'leftover': a basket of extra bread"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS5-V04","prompt":"Picture for the word 'encouraging': a coach clapping for a player"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS5-V05","prompt":"Picture for the word 'fair': a balance scale"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS5-V06","prompt":"Picture for the word 'apron': a baker in an apron"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS5-V07","prompt":"Picture for the word 'profile': a card with a photo and facts about a person"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS5-01","prompt":"A classroom Hall of Heroes wall."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS5-02","prompt":"Four everyday hero cards."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U4-LS5-03","prompt":"A medal-shaped hero profile planner."}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS5-V01","script":"civil defense. My uncle works for the civil defense."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS5-V02","script":"retired. Mrs. Amal is a retired teacher."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS5-V03","script":"leftover. He gives the leftover bread to workers."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS5-V04","script":"encouraging. Our coach is always encouraging."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS5-V05","script":"fair. A fair coach gives everyone a chance."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS5-V06","script":"apron. The baker wore a white apron."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS5-V07","script":"profile. Write a profile of your hero."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS5-T1","script":"**Card A – Uncle Fahd, civil-defense officer** · Traits: brave, calm, responsible · Examples: helped rescue families during heavy rain last winter; teaches fire-safety lessons at schools · His words: \"Stay calm – panic never helped anyone.\" **Card B – Mrs. Amal, retired teacher** · Traits: patient, generous, wise · Examples: teaches reading to neighborhood children for free every Saturday; lends books from her own shelves · Her words: \"A book is a friend that never leaves you.\" **Card C – Mr. Yousef, the baker** · Traits: hard-working, generous, kind · Examples: has baked bread six days a week for more than twenty years; gives leftover bread to street cleaners every evening · His words: \"Pay me tomorrow, my son.\" **Card D – Coach Saad** · Traits: encouraging, fair, determined · Examples: trains the school team after school even in the summer heat; gives every player a chance · His words: \"Mistakes are the first step to getting better.\""},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U4-LS5-VID","script":"Who is the hero in YOUR life? Today, you will tell the world! Read the interview notes: a civil-defense officer, a retired teacher, a baker, a coach – or interview your own hero! Every morning at five o'clock, when our street is still dark, one window is already glowing… Paragraph 1: hook + who. Paragraph 2: three traits with examples + what you learned! Publish your hero on our Hall of Heroes!"}]}],"unit_test":[{"q":"It took ___ for the shy boy to speak in front of the whole school.","answer":"courage","explanation":"Courage.","explanation_ar":"شجاعة.","options":["integrity","sacrifice","apron","courage"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","_part":"Part A – Vocabulary"},{"q":"The divers ___ the fisherman whose boat had sunk.","answer":"rescued","explanation":"Rescue.","explanation_ar":"أنقذوا.","options":["admired","retired","rescued","demonstrated"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","_part":"Part A – Vocabulary"},{"q":"She won the national prize, but she said, \"My teachers deserve it more.\" She is ___.","answer":"humble","explanation":"Humble.","explanation_ar":"متواضعة.","options":["terrified","selfish","humble","exhausted"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","_part":"Part A – Vocabulary"},{"q":"He found a wallet full of money and returned every riyal. He has ___.","answer":"integrity","explanation":"Integrity.","explanation_ar":"نزاهة.","options":["challenge","posture","suspense","integrity"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","_part":"Part A – Vocabulary"},{"q":"My older sister studies hard and helps everyone. She is my ___.","answer":"role model","explanation":"Role model.","explanation_ar":"قدوتي.","options":["flashlight","role model","launch","profile"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","_part":"Part A – Vocabulary"},{"q":"*The little boy screamed and ran when the huge dog barked.* Which word fits BEST?","answer":"terrified","explanation":"Shades of meaning.","explanation_ar":"مذعور.","options":["a bit nervous","terrified","calm","bored"],"dok":2,"skill":"shades of meaning","_part":"Part A – Vocabulary"},{"q":"Which order of happiness words goes from WEAKEST to STRONGEST?","answer":"glad → happy → thrilled","explanation":"Weak → strong.","explanation_ar":"الترتيب الصحيح.","options":["glad → happy → thrilled","thrilled → glad → happy","happy → thrilled → glad","thrilled → happy → glad"],"dok":2,"skill":"shades of meaning","_part":"Part A – Vocabulary"},{"q":"*Even after failing twice, she **persevered** and passed her driving test.* *Persevered* means ___.","answer":"kept trying even when it was hard","explanation":"Persevere.","explanation_ar":"ثابرت.","options":["kept trying even when it was hard","gave up","laughed","forgot"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary in context","_part":"Part A – Vocabulary"},{"q":"Which trait word about a volunteer is MORE exact than *nice*?","answer":"selfless","explanation":"Exact word.","explanation_ar":"selfless.","options":["good","selfless","okay","fine"],"dok":1,"skill":"word choice","_part":"Part D – Writing skills"},{"q":"Which example BEST proves that a scout is *responsible*?","answer":"He arrived at the tents at five every morning to check on elderly pilgrims.","explanation":"Specific example.","explanation_ar":"المثال الأقوى.","options":["He wears a scout scarf.","He likes Makkah.","He is a scout.","He arrived at the tents at five every morning to check on elderly pilgrims."],"dok":2,"skill":"examples","_part":"Part D – Writing skills"},{"q":"Which sentence about Faisal's father is punctuated correctly?","answer":"For example, he helped Faisal study every night.","explanation":"Comma.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["For example he helped Faisal study every night.","For, example he helped Faisal study.","For example, he helped Faisal study every night.","For example he, helped Faisal study."],"dok":2,"skill":"punctuation","_part":"Part D – Writing skills"},{"q":"After cleaning the beach for ten hours, the volunteers could hardly stand. They were ___.","answer":"exhausted","explanation":"Shades of meaning.","explanation_ar":"منهكين.","options":["a little tired","relaxed","exhausted","bored"],"dok":2,"skill":"shades of meaning","_part":"Part D – Writing skills"},{"q":"Which sentence SHOWS that a volunteer is kind instead of telling it?","answer":"She knelt down, wiped the lost child's tears and held his hand until his mother came.","explanation":"Show, don't tell.","explanation_ar":"يُظهر اللطف.","options":["She is very kind.","She knelt down, wiped the lost child's tears and held his hand until his mother came.","She is a kind volunteer.","Kindness is her trait."],"dok":3,"skill":"show, don't tell","_part":"Part D – Writing skills"},{"q":"Which is the strongest CONCLUSION for a text about a volunteer hero?","answer":"She taught me that the best way to be happy is to make someone else happy.","explanation":"Conclusion.","explanation_ar":"أقوى خاتمة.","options":["She taught me that the best way to be happy is to make someone else happy.","She has a blue scarf.","She lives in Jeddah.","That is the end of my text."],"dok":3,"skill":"conclusions","_part":"Part D – Writing skills"}],"unit_writing":{"task":"Write a two-paragraph descriptive text (120–150 words) about a real hero in your community – for example, a volunteer, a teacher, a neighbor or a family member. Paragraph 1: a hook and who your hero is. Paragraph 2: three exact traits, each with a specific example, transitions and a conclusion about what you learned.","model":"While most people are still asleep on Friday mornings, my aunt Reem is already on the beach with a bag in her hand. She is a volunteer, and she is my hero. (new paragraph) First, she is determined. For example, she has organized a beach clean-up every month for three years, even in the summer heat. She is also generous with her time. Every Ramadan, she spends her evenings packing iftar meals for workers in our neighborhood. Above all, she is encouraging. When I complained that one person can't change much, she smiled and said, \"Every bag of rubbish is one less in the sea.\" Aunt Reem has taught me that small actions, repeated again and again, can make a big difference.","marks":20}});
